## 2. Design Goals

| Goal | Target | Strategy |
|------|--------|----------|
| Frame budget | < 16ms per frame during drag/resize/rotate | requestAnimationFrame loop, local Zustand state (no Apollo round-trip during drag), CSS transforms (GPU-accelerated) |
| Cross-device input | Pointer Events API (mouse, touch, pen) | `onPointerDown/Move/Up` instead of `onMouseDown/Move/Up`; `setPointerCapture` for tracking outside element bounds |
| Undo/redo robustness | Command pattern with inverse operations | History stack max 50 entries, auto-coalescing consecutive position changes into single undo entry |
| Snap accuracy | Pixel-accurate alignment within 5px threshold | Threshold-based proximity detection (not collision detection); guide lines rendered as SVG overlays |
| Element count support | Smooth with 5-30 elements (typical), 50 max | `React.memo` per element keyed by `id` — no virtualization (virtualization breaks absolute positioning + hit-testing). Elements outside viewport get `visibility: hidden` via IntersectionObserver only above 50 elements |
| Accessibility | Keyboard navigation for all operations | Full keyboard shortcut suite; ARIA roles on canvas + elements; focus management prevents shortcut capture by inputs; SR live announcements for drag/resize deltas |

---

## 3. Key Design Decisions

### 3.1 Rendering Approach: CSS-Positioned DIVs (NOT SVG/Canvas API)

| Option | Accessibility | DOM Events | Performance | Text Rendering | Decision |
|--------|---------------|-------------|-------------|----------------|----------|
| CSS-positioned divs | ✅ Native ARIA, screen reader | ✅ Native pointer events | ⚠️ ~100 elements fine | ✅ Native text, editable | **CHOSEN** |
| SVG elements | ✅ ARIA on SVG nodes | ✅ Native events | ✅ Efficient | ⚠️ Text needs `<text>` elements | Rejected — no text editing |
| HTML Canvas API | ❌ No DOM, no ARIA | ❌ Hit-testing manual | ✅ Fast for 1000s | ❌ Manual text rendering | Rejected — poor accessibility |

**Rationale:** Certificate templates have < 50 elements. CSS divs give native accessibility, native DOM event handling, and natural text editing via `contentEditable`. Performance with < 100 elements is not a concern with proper React optimization (memo, virtualization not needed at this scale).

### 3.2 Input API: Pointer Events (NOT Mouse Events)

| Concern | Pointer Events | Mouse Events |
|---------|---------------|--------------|
| Touch devices | ✅ Unified handling | ❌ Needs separate touch handlers |
| Pen/stylus | ✅ Pressure, tilt data | ❌ Not available |
| Capture | ✅ `setPointerCapture` tracks outside bounds | ⚠️ Needs `window` listener workaround |
| Browser support | ✅ > 97% global | ✅ Universal |

**Decision:** Use Pointer Events API exclusively. `e.clientX/clientY` are available on all pointer events for coordinate calculations. Call `setPointerCapture(e.pointerId)` on pointer down to maintain tracking when cursor leaves the element.

### 3.3 State Management: Zustand Session Store + Debounced GraphQL Saves

| State Type | Location | Persistence | Sync |
|------------|----------|-------------|------|
| Live element positions (during drag) | Zustand `canvasStore` | None (session-only) | Never saved during drag — only on pointer up |
| Saved element state | Apollo cache (GraphQL query) | Normalized cache | Saved via mutation on pointer up / save button |
| Undo/redo history | Zustand `canvasStore.history[]` | None (session-only) | Re-applied to Zustand state, then optionally saved |
| Zoom/pan/grid UI state | Zustand `canvasStore` | None (session-only) | Never saved |

**isDirty Protocol:**
- Any mutation to `elements[]` (position, size, rotation, add, delete) sets `isDirty = true`
- User clicks Save → all unsaved changes flushed via GraphQL mutations → `isDirty = false`
- User navigates away with `isDirty = true` → browser `beforeunload` confirmation prompt
- Debounce: position updates batch 300ms before GraphQL mutation (only on `pointerup`, not automatic)

### 3.4 History/Undo: Command Pattern

Each user action pushed onto `history` stack as a command object with `execute()` and `inverse()`:

| Command Type | execute() | inverse() |
|--------------|-----------|-----------|
| `MoveElement` | Set element x/y to new values | Set element x/y to old values |
| `ResizeElement` | Set width/height/x/y to new values | Set width/height/x/y to old values |
| `RotateElement` | Set rotation to new value | Set rotation to old value |
| `AddElement` | Add element to elements[] | Remove element from elements[] |
| `DeleteElement` | Remove element from elements[] | Add element back to elements[] |
| `DuplicateElement` | Add element with offset | Remove duplicated element |

**Coalescing rule:** Consecutive `MoveElement` commands for the same element within 500ms are merged into a single command (store only the earliest old position). This prevents 50 undo steps for a single drag gesture.

**Stack limits:** `history` max 50 entries; `redoHistory` cleared on any new non-undo/redo command.

### 3.5 Snap Algorithm: Threshold-Based Proximity (NOT Grid Collision)

Grid snap and element-alignment snap share a proximity-detection approach rather than collision detection:

| Snap Type | Trigger | Threshold | Algorithm |
|-----------|---------|-----------|-----------|
| Grid snap | Grid enabled + element being dragged | gridSize (default 10px) | `snapped = Math.round(value / gridSize) * gridSize` |
| Element alignment (vertical) | Element center/edges within 5px of another element's center/edges | 5px | Compare dragged element's left/centerX/right against all others' left/centerX/right |
| Element alignment (horizontal) | Same threshold for top/centerY/bottom | 5px | Compare top/centerY/bottom |

**Guide rendering:** When snap threshold is met, render an SVG `<line>` as overlay on `SnapGuideOverlay`. Remove guide when drag ends.

---

### 4.1 CanvasElement Type (Unified Discriminated Union)

Per INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS.md §2, the element type enum aligns with `CertificateElementType`:
`static_text`, `data_text`, `data_date`, `image`, `qr_code`, `shape` (6 values).

The `CanvasElement` is a discriminated union — no `props: Record<string, unknown>` bag.

```
type CanvasElement =
  | { id: string; type: 'static_text'; x, y, width, height: number; rotation: number; zIndex: number;
      content: string; fontFamily: string; fontSize: number; fontWeight: number; fontStyle: 'normal'|'italic';
      color: string; align: 'left'|'center'|'right'; lineHeight: number; }
  | { id: string; type: 'data_text'; x, y, width, height, rotation, zIndex: number;
      variableId: string; placeholderText: string; fontFamily, fontSize, fontWeight: number;
      fontStyle: 'normal'|'italic'; color: string; align: 'left'|'center'|'right'; lineHeight: number; }
  | { id: string; type: 'data_date'; x, y, width, height, rotation, zIndex: number;
      variableId: string; dateFormat: string; fontFamily, fontSize, fontWeight: number;
      color: string; align: 'left'|'center'|'right'; }
  | { id: string; type: 'image'; x, y, width, height, rotation, zIndex: number;
      src: string; fit: 'cover'|'contain'|'fill'; opacity: number; borderRadius: number; }
  | { id: string; type: 'qr_code'; x, y, width, height, rotation, zIndex: number;
      contentVariableId: string; errorCorrection: 'L'|'M'|'Q'|'H'; }
  | { id: string; type: 'shape'; x, y, width, height, rotation, zIndex: number;
      shapeType: 'rectangle'|'ellipse'|'line'; fillColor: string; strokeColor: string;
      strokeWidth: number; borderRadius: number; }
```

Each union member has `id`, `type`, `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, `rotation`, `zIndex` as common fields, then type-specific properties inline.

### 4.2 Complete Component Hierarchy with Prop Interfaces

```
CanvasContainer (frontend/common/views/dashboard/cert-canvas/canvasContainer.tsx)
  props: { templateId: string; locale: string; permissions: string[] }
  → calls useCanvasViewModel(templateId) → passes result to CanvasView
  → CanvasView (switcher) → ResponsiveViewSwitch → lazy desktop/mobile
```

#### CanvasContainer

```
interface CanvasContainerProps {
  templateId: string;
  locale: string;
  permissions: readonly string[];
}
```

#### useCanvasViewModel return type

```
interface CanvasViewModel {
  // Apollo query state
  template: Template | null;
  loading: boolean;
  error: ApolloError | undefined;

  // Store state (mapped from Zustand selectors)
  elements: CanvasElement[];
  selectedIds: string[];
  zoomLevel: number;
  panOffset: { x: number; y: number };
  isGridEnabled: boolean;
  gridSize: number;
  showRulers: boolean;
  snapToGrid: boolean;
  isDirty: boolean;
  canUndo: boolean;
  canRedo: boolean;
  interactionState: InteractionState;
  activeGuides: GuideLine[];
  clipboard: CanvasElement[];

  // Actions
  selectElement: (id: string, additive: boolean) => void;
  selectMultiple: (ids: string[]) => void;
  selectAll: () => void;
  clearSelection: () => void;
  addElement: (element: CanvasElement) => void;
  updateElementPosition: (id: string, x: number, y: number) => void;
  commitPositionChange: (id: string, oldX: number, oldY: number) => void;
  updateElementSize: (id: string, w: number, h: number, x?: number, y?: number) => void;
  commitResizeChange: (id: string, oldState: CanvasElement) => void;
  updateElementRotation: (id: string, rotation: number) => void;
  commitRotationChange: (id: string, oldAngle: number) => void;
  deleteSelection: () => void;
  duplicateSelection: () => void;
  copySelection: () => void;
  paste: () => void;
  bringToFront: (id: string) => void;
  sendToBack: (id: string) => void;
  reorderElement: (id: string, newIndex: number) => void;
  undo: () => void;
  redo: () => void;
  setZoom: (zoom: number) => void;
  setPanOffset: (offset: { x: number; y: number }) => void;
  setTool: (tool: canvasTool) => void;
  setGridSize: (size: number) => void;
  toggleGrid: () => void;
  toggleSnap: () => void;
  toggleRulers: () => void;
  setActiveGuides: (guides: GuideLine[]) => void;
  setInteractionState: (state: InteractionState) => void;
  save: () => Promise<void>;
  resetTransform: () => void;
  fitToScreen: () => void;
}
```

#### CanvasDesktopView

```
interface CanvasDesktopViewProps {
  vm: CanvasViewModel;
  t: TranslationFunctions['dashboard']['certificatesCanvas'];
}
```

Layout: `Box` with `display: flex; flexDirection: column; height: 100vh`
- Top: `CanvasToolbar` (fixed 56px height)
- Middle: `Box` with `display: flex; flex: 1; overflow: hidden`
  - Left: `LeftPanel` (280px width, collapsible)
  - Center: `CanvasViewport` (flex: 1)
  - Right: `PropertyPanel` (320px width, collapsible)

#### CanvasMobileView

```
interface CanvasMobileViewProps {
  vm: CanvasViewModel;
  t: TranslationFunctions['dashboard']['certificatesCanvas'];
}
```

Layout: `Box` with `display: flex; flexDirection: column; height: 100dvh`
- Top: Simplified toolbar (add element FAB, zoom only)
- Center: `TransformWrapper` canvas (read-only on mobile — no drag, no resize, no rotate)
- Bottom: `BottomSheet` for properties (conditional — when element selected, tappable to expand)
- Threshold: Below width 1024px → mobile view. Mobile is read-only preview + "Edit on desktop" banner.

#### CanvasToolbar (desktop top bar)

```
interface CanvasToolbarProps {
  zoomLevel: number;
  isGridEnabled: boolean;
  showRulers: boolean;
  snapToGrid: boolean;
  isDirty: boolean;
  isSaving: boolean;
  canUndo: boolean;
  canRedo: boolean;
  onAddElement: (type: CertificateElementType) => void;
  onZoomIn: () => void;
  onZoomOut: () => void;
  onFitToScreen: () => void;
  onResetZoom: () => void;
  onToggleGrid: () => void;
  onToggleRulers: () => void;
  onToggleSnap: () => void;
  onUndo: () => void;
  onRedo: () => void;
  onSave: () => void;
  t: CanvasToolbarTranslations;
}
```

Toolbar groups (left to right, separated by `<Divider orientation="vertical" />`):
1. **File menu** (`<Menu>`): Save (`SaveOutlined`), Export (out of scope — Plan 15)
2. **Edit menu** (`<Menu>`): Undo (`UndoOutlined`), Redo (`RedoOutlined`), Delete (`DeleteOutlined`), Duplicate (`ContentCopyOutlined`)
3. **Add element** (`<Menu>`): Text (`TextFieldsOutlined`), Image (`ImageOutlined`), QR Code (`QrCodeOutlined`), Shape (`CategoryOutlined`), Date (`CalendarTodayOutlined`)
4. **View toggles**: Grid (`GridOnOutlined`/`GridOffOutlined`), Rulers (`StraightenOutlined`), Snap (`GridOnOutlined`)
5. **Zoom controls**: Zoom In (`ZoomInOutlined`), Zoom %, Zoom Out (`ZoomOutOutlined`), Fit (`FitScreenOutlined`), Reset (`CenterFocusStrongOutlined`)
6. **Save button**: `SaveOutlined` — disabled when `!isDirty`, loading when `isSaving`

#### LeftPanel (desktop left sidebar)

```
interface LeftPanelProps {
  elements: CanvasElement[];
  selectedIds: string[];
  onAddElement: (type: CertificateElementType) => void;
  onSelectElement: (id: string, additive: boolean) => void;
  onReorderElement: (id: string, newIndex: number) => void;
  onBringToFront: (id: string) => void;
  onSendToBack: (id: string) => void;
  t: LeftPanelTranslations;
}
```

Sections:
1. **Element type buttons** (top, vertical `Stack`): 5 buttons matching toolbar add-elements
2. **Layer list** (bottom, scrollable): Each row = `LayerListItem` showing element type icon, name/label, visibility eye toggle, z-order drag handle. Uses `@dnd-kit/sortable` for drag-to-reorder (Plan 12 feature, scaffolded here).

#### PropertyPanel (desktop right sidebar)

```
interface PropertyPanelProps {
  selectedElements: CanvasElement[];
  onUpdateElement: (id: string, patch: Partial<CanvasElement>) => void;
  onDelete: () => void;
  onDuplicate: () => void;
  t: PropertyPanelTranslations;
}
```

Sections (conditional):
- **No selection**: Empty state (`Typography` — "Select an element to edit its properties")
- **Single selection**: Full property editor (position, size, rotation, type-specific)
- **Multi selection**: Group bounding box info + count, alignment buttons (left/center/right/top/middle/bottom)

Property fields by element type (see §10 Element Rendering below for details).

#### CanvasSurface (shared — the zoomable canvas)

```
interface CanvasSurfaceProps {
  width: number;   // Template px (e.g., 794 for A4 at 96 DPI)
  height: number;  // Template px (e.g., 1123 for A4 at 96 DPI)
  zoom: number;
  backgroundImageUrl: string | null;
  elements: CanvasElement[];
  selectedIds: string[];
  interactionState: InteractionState;
  activeGuides: GuideLine[];
  isGridEnabled: boolean;
  gridSize: number;
  isInteractive: boolean;
  onElementPointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent, elementId: string) => void;
  onCanvasPointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent) => void;
  onResizeHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent, handle: ResizeHandleType) => void;
  onRotationHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent) => void;
  t: CanvasSurfaceTranslations;
}
```

Renders inside `<TransformComponent>` — the react-zoom-pan-pinch child. Contains:
- `backgroundImageLayer` (absolute fill)
- `elementRenderer[]` (absolute positioned per element)
- `selectionFrame` (conditional — single selection only)
- `snapGuideOverlay` (conditional grid + alignment guides)
- `marqueeSelection` (conditional — during marquee interaction)

#### ElementRenderer (shared — renders a single element)

```
interface ElementRendererProps {
  element: CanvasElement;
  isSelected: boolean;
  isInteractive: boolean;
  zoom: number;
  onPointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent) => void;
}
```

Renders: `position: absolute; left: element.x; top: element.y; width: element.width; height: element.height; transform: rotate(${element.rotation}deg); zIndex: element.zIndex;`

Content rendering: `switch(element.type)` → text span, image img, QR placeholder div, shape div, date span. Delegates to Plan 10/12 element components for visual rendering.

Memoized with `React.memo` — re-renders only when `element` reference changes (Zustand selector returns new ref on position update).

#### SelectionFrame (shared)

```
interface SelectionFrameProps {
  element: CanvasElement;
  zoom: number;
  isMulti: boolean;  // true when selectedIds.length > 1
  onResizeHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent, handle: ResizeHandleType) => void;
  onRotationHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent) => void;
}
```

Renders:
- 2px solid outline using `theme.palette.primary.main` (NOT hardcoded blue)
- Optional `ResizeHandles` (8 handles) when `!isMulti`
- Optional `RotationHandle` when `!isMulti`
- Optional `GroupBoundingBox` (dashed) when `isMulti`

#### ResizeHandles (shared)

```
interface ResizeHandlesProps {
  element: CanvasElement;
  zoom: number;
  onHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent, handle: ResizeHandleType) => void;
}

type ResizeHandleType = 'nw' | 'n' | 'ne' | 'e' | 'se' | 's' | 'sw' | 'w';
```

8 handles: 10px squares with `theme.palette.background.paper` fill + 1px `theme.palette.primary.main` border. Cursor styles per handle: `nwse-resize`, `ns-resize`, `nesw-resize`, `ew-resize`, etc.

**v1 constraint:** Resize handles are disabled when `element.rotation !== 0` (resize-while-rotated is a v2 feature). Show a tooltip: "Resize not available while rotated".

#### RotationHandle (shared)

```
interface RotationHandleProps {
  element: CanvasElement;
  zoom: number;
  onHandlePointerDown: (e: React.PointerEvent) => void;
}
```

12px circle positioned 30px above element's top-center. Connected by 2px vertical line using `theme.palette.primary.main`. Cursor: `crosshair`. Shows angle tooltip during rotation.

#### ZoomControls (desktop toolbar sub-component)

```
interface ZoomControlsProps {
  zoom: number;
  onZoomIn: () => void;
  onZoomOut: () => void;
  onFitToScreen: () => void;
  onResetZoom: () => void;
  t: ZoomControlsTranslations;
}
```

#### CanvasRuler (shared)

```
interface CanvasRulerProps {
  orientation: 'horizontal' | 'vertical';
  length: number;    // In template px
  zoom: number;
  panOffset: number; // Scroll offset for sync
}
```

Markings every 50 template px (major ticks with number labels, minor ticks every 10px). Background: `theme.palette.background.default`. Border: `theme.palette.divider`.

#### MarqueeSelection (shared)

```
interface MarqueeSelectionProps {
  rect: { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number } | null;
}
```

Renders semi-transparent rectangle using `theme.palette.primary.main` at 20% opacity with dashed border.

### 4.3 Component Responsibilities Summary

| Component | Responsibility | Reads from Store | Writes to Store |
|-----------|---------------|-------------------|-----------------|
| CanvasContainer | Fetches template data, calls ViewModel, passes to switcher | None | None |
| useCanvasViewModel | All business logic: Apollo queries/mutations, store access, handlers | All | All |
| canvas.desktop.tsx | Desktop layout: toolbar + left + canvas + right | vm props | vm actions |
| canvas.mobile.tsx | Mobile layout: read-only preview + "Edit on desktop" banner | vm props | None |
| CanvasToolbar | Renders toolbar buttons, dispatches actions | zoom, grid, snap, rulers, isDirty, isSaving, canUndo, canRedo | setZoom, toggleGrid, toggleSnap, toggleRulers, undo, redo, save, addElement |
| LeftPanel | Element type buttons + layer list | elements, selectedIds | selectElement, reorderElement, bringToFront, sendToBack |
| CanvasSurface | Renders at template dimensions, hosts all canvas layers | zoom, elements, selectedIds, interactionState, guides | setInteractionState (via callbacks) |
| ElementRenderer | Renders single element at position with styling | element | None (read-only display) |
| SelectionFrame | Shows selection border + handles/bounding box | selectedIds, element | None |
| ResizeHandles | 8 drag handles for resizing | selectedElement | updateElementSize |
| RotationHandle | Rotation dial above element | selectedElement | updateElementRotation |
| PropertyPanel | Edits selected element properties | selectedElements | updateElement |
| CanvasRuler | Pixel ruler with zoom/sync | zoom, panOffset | None |
| SnapGuideOverlay | Grid dots + alignment guide lines | isGridEnabled, gridSize, activeGuides | None |
| MarqueeSelection | Rubber-band rectangle | interactionState (marquee rect) | None |
| ZoomControls | Zoom in/out/fit/reset buttons | zoom | setZoom |

---

## 5. Zustand Canvas Store Design

### 5.1 Store Location

`frontend/common/stores/certCanvasStore.ts`

Per `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md`: uses `create<CanvasStoreState>(set => ({...}))` pattern. No `persist` — canvas state is session-only (ephemeral editing session). No `Set<string>` — use `string[]` for serializeability.

### 5.2 Complete State Shape

| State Field | Type | Default | Description |
|-------------|------|---------|-------------|
| `elements` | `readonly CanvasElement[]` | `[]` | Current (possibly unsaved) element state with position, size, rotation, zIndex |
| `savedElements` | `readonly CanvasElement[]` | `[]` | Snapshot of last-saved state (for dirty diff comparison) |
| `selectedIds` | `readonly string[]` | `[]` | Element IDs currently selected (NOT Set — follows store convention) |
| `clipboard` | `readonly CanvasElement[]` | `[]` | Copy/paste buffer |
| `interactionState` | `InteractionState` | `{ type: 'idle' }` | Current interaction type |
| `zoomLevel` | `number` | `1.0` | 0.25 – 4.0 (25% — 400%) |
| `panOffset` | `{ x: number; y: number }` | `{ x: 0, y: 0 }` | Scroll offset of viewport |
| `tool` | `CanvasTool` | `'select'` | Active tool (select, add-text, add-image, marquee) |
| `isGridEnabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Grid overlay toggle |
| `gridSize` | `number` | `10` | Grid spacing in template px |
| `showRulers` | `boolean` | `true` | Show/hide rulers |
| `snapToGrid` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether grid snapping is active |
| `snapToElements` | `boolean` | `true` | Whether element-alignment snapping is active |
| `isPanning` | `boolean` | `false` | Spacebar+drag or middle mouse active |
| `past` | `Command[]` | `[]` | Undo stack (max 50) |
| `future` | `Command[]` | `[]` | Redo stack |
| `isDirty` | `boolean` | `false` | Unsaved changes exist |
| `isSaving` | `boolean` | `false` | Save mutation in flight |
| `activeGuides` | `readonly GuideLine[]` | `[]` | Currently visible snap guides (cleared on drag end) |
| `canvasFocus` | `boolean` | `false` | Canvas focused (shortcuts active — false when typing in inputs) |
| `expectedVersion` | `number` | `0` | Optimistic locking version from server (for bulk save) |

### 5.3 InteractionState Discriminated Union

```
type InteractionState =
  | { type: 'idle' }
  | { type: 'dragging'; elementIds: string[]; startX: number; startY: number;
      originalPositions: Array<{ id: string; x: number; y: number }> }
  | { type: 'resizing'; elementId: string; handle: ResizeHandleType;
      startX: number; startY: number; originalState: CanvasElement }
  | { type: 'rotating'; elementId: string; startX: number; startY: number; originalAngle: number }
  | { type: 'marquee'; startX: number; startY: number; currentX: number; currentY: number }
  | { type: 'panning'; startX: number; startY: number; originalPanX: number; originalPanY: number }
```

### 5.4 CanvasTool Enum

```
type CanvasTool = 'select' | 'add-static_text' | 'add-data_text' | 'add-image' | 'add-qr_code' | 'add-shape' | 'add-data_date';
```

### 5.5 Complete Actions (26 total)

| Action | Parameters | Returns | Side Effects |
|--------|------------|---------|--------------|
| `selectElement` | `id: string, additive: boolean` | `void` | If additive: toggle in selectedIds. Else: selectedIds = [id] |
| `selectMultiple` | `ids: string[]` | `void` | selectedIds = ids |
| `selectAll` | `void` | `void` | selectedIds = elements.map(e => e.id) |
| `clearSelection` | `void` | `void` | selectedIds = [] |
| `addElement` | `element: CanvasElement` | `void` | Push AddElement command to past[], elements += element, isDirty = true, select new element |
| `updateElementPosition` | `id: string, x: number, y: number` | `void` | Update element x/y in elements[] (live, no command — use rAF) |
| `commitPositionChange` | `id: string, oldX: number, oldY: number` | `void` | Push MoveElement command to past[] (with 500ms coalescing), isDirty = true |
| `updateElementSize` | `id: string, w: number, h: number, x?: number, y?: number` | `void` | Update width/height (and x/y for corner handles) — live, no command |
| `commitResizeChange` | `id: string, oldState: CanvasElement` | `void` | Push ResizeElement command to past[], isDirty = true |
| `updateElementRotation` | `id: string, rotation: number` | `void` | Update rotation — live, no command |
| `commitRotationChange` | `id: string, oldAngle: number` | `void` | Push RotateElement command to past[], isDirty = true |
| `deleteSelection` | `void` | `void` | Remove selected from elements[], push DeleteElement command, clear selectedIds, isDirty = true |
| `duplicateSelection` | `void` | `void` | Clone selected with +20px offset, new UUIDs, push DuplicateElement commands, isDirty = true, select new clones |
| `copySelection` | `void` | `void` | clipboard = deepClone(selectedElements) |
| `paste` | `void` | `void` | Clone clipboard items with +20px, new UUIDs, add AddElement commands, isDirty = true, select new clones |
| `bringToFront` | `id: string` | `void` | Set element zIndex = max + 1, push ReorderCommand, renormalize zIndex array, isDirty = true |
| `sendToBack` | `id: string` | `void` | Set element zIndex = min - 1, push ReorderCommand, renormalize zIndex array, isDirty = true |
| `reorderElement` | `id: string, newIndex: number` | `void` | Reorder elements[], renormalize zIndex, push ReorderCommand, isDirty = true |
| `undo` | `void` | `void` | Pop past[], execute inverse, push to future[] |
| `redo` | `void` | `void` | Pop future[], execute, push to past[] |
| `setZoom` | `zoom: number` | `void` | Clamp to 0.25–4.0 |
| `setPanOffset` | `offset: { x: number; y: number }` | `void` | Updates panOffset |
| `setTool` | `tool: CanvasTool` | `void` | Updates tool |
| `setGridSize` | `size: number` | `void` | Updates gridSize |
| `toggleGrid` | `void` | `void` | Toggles isGridEnabled |
| `toggleSnap` | `void` | `void` | Toggles snapToGrid |
| `toggleRulers` | `void` | `void` | Toggles showRulers |
| `setInteractionState` | `state: InteractionState` | `void` | Updates interactionState |
| `setActiveGuides` | `guides: GuideLine[]` | `void` | Updates activeGuides for overlay |
| `setCanvasFocus` | `focus: boolean` | `void` | Updates canvasFocus |
| `markDirty` | `void` | `void` | isDirty = true |
| `markSaved` | `void` | `void` | savedElements = deepClone(elements), isDirty = false, isSaving = false |
| `setSaving` | `bool: boolean` | `void` | isSaving = bool |
| `resetToSaved` | `void` | `void` | elements = deepClone(savedElements), past = [], future = [], isDirty = false |
| `setExpectedVersion` | `version: number` | `void` | Updates expectedVersion (from server response) |

### 5.6 zIndex Renormalization

After `bringToFront`, `sendToBack`, or `reorderElement`, the store renormalizes all `zIndex` values to sequential integers starting at 0:

```
elements = elements
  .sort((a, b) => a.zIndex - b.zIndex)
  .map((e, i) => ({ ...e, zIndex: i }))
```

This prevents zIndex overflow and keeps the array deterministic.

### 5.7 Computed Selectors (non-stored, derived via `useCanvasStore` selectors)

| Selector | Derivation |
|----------|------------|
| `selectedElements` | `elements.filter(e => selectedIds.includes(e.id))` |
| `groupBoundingBox` | `{ minX, minY, maxX, maxY }` from selected elements' x/y/w/h |
| `canUndo` | `past.length > 0` |
| `canRedo` | `future.length > 0` |
| `hasUnsavedChanges` | `JSON.stringify(elements) !== JSON.stringify(savedElements)` |
| `selectedCount` | `selectedIds.length` |

### 5.8 History Stack Protocol (past[] / present / future[] pattern)

```
User Action (e.g., drag end)
  │
  ├─ If coalescing (same element + same command type + < 500ms since last):
  │    └─ Replace top of past[] with merged command (keep earliest oldPosition)
  │
  └─ If not coalescing:
       ├─ past.push(newCommand)
       ├─ if past.length > 50 → past.shift()
       └─ future = []  (clear redo on any new command)

Undo:
  │
  ├─ const cmd = past.pop()
  ├─ cmd.inverse()  (applies old state to elements[])
  └─ future.push(cmd)

Redo:
  │
  ├─ const cmd = future.pop()
  ├─ cmd.execute()  (re-applies new state)
  └─ past.push(cmd)
```

### 5.9 Save Protocol (Optimistic Locking + Diff-Only Payload)

On `save()`:
1. `setSaving(true)`
2. Compute diff: compare `elements` vs `savedElements` → only send changed elements
3. Call `updateTemplateElementsBulk` mutation with:
   - `templateId: string`
   - `expectedVersion: number` (from store `expectedVersion`)
   - `changes: Array<{ id: string; x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number; rotation: number; zIndex: number; ...typeSpecificProps }>`
4. On success: `markSaved()`, `setExpectedVersion(response.version)`, toast success
5. On optimistic lock failure (version mismatch): toast error, refetch template, `resetToSaved()`
6. On other error: toast error, `setSaving(false)` (isDirty stays true)

---

## 6. Coordinate System

### 6.1 Two Coordinate Spaces

| Space | Origin | Units | Used By |
|-------|--------|-------|---------|
| **Template Space** | Top-left of canvas (0, 0) | Template pixels at 96 DPI (e.g., 794×1123 for A4 portrait) | Element positions, sizes, rotation, storage |
| **Screen Space** | Top-left of canvas viewport | CSS pixels with zoom + pan applied | Pointer events, rendering |

**DPI convention:** 96 DPI is the canonical unit for template pixels (per INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS §18 — aligned with Plan 6's Puppeteer renderer and Plan 10's template definition). This resolves the 72-vs-96 conflict — 96 DPI (CSS px) is both the template coordinate unit and the screen rendering unit, making conversion trivial (1:1 at zoom=1).

### 6.2 Conversion Functions

| Function | Signature | Used When |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| `screenToTemplate` | `(screenX, screenY, zoom, panOffset) → {tx, ty}` | Pointer down/move → update element position |
| `templateToScreen` | `(templateX, templateY, zoom, panOffset) → {sx, sy}` | Render ruler markings, guide positions |

**Conversion formulas:**
- `templateX = (screenX - panOffset.x) / zoom`
- `screenX = templateX * zoom + panOffset.x`
- Same for Y axis

**Full implementation in `canvasUtils.ts`:**

```typescript
export function screenToTemplate(
  clientX: number,
  clientY: number,
  containerRect: DOMRect,
  panOffset: { x: number; y: number },
  zoom: number
): { x: number; y: number } {
  return {
    x: (clientX - containerRect.left - panOffset.x) / zoom,
    y: (clientY - containerRect.top - panOffset.y) / zoom,
  };
}

export function templateToScreen(
  templateX: number,
  templateY: number,
  containerRect: DOMRect,
  panOffset: { x: number; y: number },
  zoom: number
): { x: number; y: number } {
  return {
    x: templateX * zoom + containerRect.left + panOffset.x,
    y: templateY * zoom + containerRect.top + panOffset.y,
  };
}
```

### 6.3 Zoom Application via react-zoom-pan-pinch

Per `node_research/react-zoom-pan-pinch.md`, canvas zoom and pan are handled by `react-zoom-pan-pinch` v4.0.3's `TransformWrapper` and `TransformComponent` components.

**TransformWrapper configuration:**
- `minScale: 0.25` (25% minimum zoom)
- `maxScale: 4.0` (400% maximum zoom)
- `limitToBounds: true` (prevents panning beyond canvas edges)
- `wheel: { step: 0.1 }` (smooth wheel zoom — 10% per notch)
- `doubleClick: { mode: 'zoomIn', step: 0.7 }` (double-click to zoom in)
- `panning: { velocityDisabled: false }` (smooth pan momentum on desktop)

**TransformComponent configuration:**
- `wrapperClass: "canvas-transform-wrapper"`
- `contentClass: "canvas-transform-content"`
- Children: `CanvasSurface` (the canvas with elements)

**Imperative ref (`ReactZoomPanPanPinchRef`):**
The `useCanvasZoomPan` hook holds a ref to the `TransformWrapper` for programmatic control:
- `ref.current.zoomIn(step)` — toolbar zoom in button
- `ref.current.zoomOut(step)` — toolbar zoom out button
- `ref.current.setTransform(x, y, scale)` — set exact pan/zoom
- `ref.current.resetTransform()` — reset to 100% zoom, 0,0 pan
- `ref.current.centerView()` — fit-to-screen
- `ref.current.zoomToElement(element, scale)` — zoom to specific element

**State sync:** TransformWrapper's `onTransformed` callback writes `scale`, `positionX`, `positionY` to the Zustand store's `zoomLevel` and `panOffset`. Store actions (`setZoom`, `setPanOffset`) call ref methods for programmatic changes.

**Scale on canvas children:** TransformWrapper handles the scale transform internally — instead of manually applying `transform: scale(zoomLevel)` on CanvasSurface, the TransformComponent wraps the surface in a div with the appropriate CSS transform. This means ElementRenderer and other canvas children render at natural template-pixel coordinates and the wrapper handles the visual scale.

### 6.4 Pan Constraints

Pan is constrained by `limitToBounds: true` on TransformWrapper — the canvas cannot be dragged outside the viewport. This replaces the manual `scrollLeft/scrollTop` approach with the library's built-in boundary detection.

| Zoom Level | Scale | Canvas 794px width renders as |
|------------|-------|-------------------------------|
| 25% | 0.25 | 198.5px on screen |
| 50% | 0.5 | 397px on screen |
| 100% | 1.0 | 794px |
| 200% | 2.0 | 1588px |
| 400% | 4.0 | 3176px |

---

## 7. Interaction State Machine

### 7.1 State Transitions

```
                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
                    │              IDLE                         │
                    └──────┬──────┬──────┬──────┬──────┬────────┘
                           │      │      │      │      │
              ┌────────────┘      │      │      │      └────────────┐
              ▼                   ▼      │      ▼                   ▼
     ELEMENT_CLICK          CANVAS_CLICK │ RESIZE_HANDLE   ROTATION_HANDLE
              │                   │      │      │                   │
              ▼                   │      ▼      ▼                   ▼
         SELECTING           DESELECT   RESIZING                  ROTATING
              │                   │                                      │
   ┌─────┴─────┘                 │                                      │
   ▼             ▼               │                                      │
 DRAGGING    MARQUEE             │                                      │
 (pointer     (pointer on        │                                      │
  on          empty              │                                      │
 element)     canvas)           │                                      │
   │             │              │                                      │
   ▼             ▼              │                                      │
 (pointer       (pointer         │                                      │
  up → save)    up → select)    ▼                                      ▼
              ALL TRANSITIONS RETURN TO IDLE ON pointerup
```

| State | Entry Trigger | Active Cursor | Exit Trigger |
|-------|---------------|---------------|--------------|
| `idle` | Initial / after any action completes | `default` | Pointer down on element/handle/canvas |
| `dragging` | Pointer down on element body | `move` | Pointer up |
| `resizing` | Pointer down on resize handle | `nwse-resize` / `nesw-resize` / `ns-resize` / `ew-resize` | Pointer up |
| `rotating` | Pointer down on rotation handle | `grab` → `grabbing` | Pointer up |
| `marquee` | Pointer down on empty canvas | `crosshair` | Pointer up |
| `panning` | Spacebar+pointer down or middle mouse down | `grab` → `grabbing` | Pointer up / spacebar up |

### 7.2 Multi-Select Mode Override

When `selectedIds.length > 1`, clicking on an already-selected element enters `dragging` (group move) instead of `selecting`. Clicking on an unselected element clears old selection and selects only that element, unless Ctrl/Cmd is held (additive selection).

---

## 8. Snap Algorithms

### 8.1 Grid Snap (REQ-11-07)

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Enabled | `isGridEnabled` from store |
| Grid size | `gridSize` (default 10 template px) |
| Application | Only during `dragging` and `resizing` states |
| Snap formula | `snapped = Math.round(value / gridSize) * gridSize` |

Grid snap applies to element `x` and `y` during drag, and to `width`/`height` during resize (rounded to grid granularity).

### 8.2 Element Alignment Snap (REQ-11-08)

**Reference points per element:**
- Vertical: `x` (left edge), `x + width/2` (center), `x + width` (right edge)
- Horizontal: `y` (top edge), `y + height/2` (center), `y + height` (bottom edge)

**Algorithm (per drag frame):**

| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 1 | Get dragged element's 6 reference points (3 vertical, 3 horizontal) |
| 2 | For each other element on canvas, get their 6 reference points |
| 3 | For each pair (dragged ref vs other ref), compute absolute difference |
| 4 | If any difference < threshold (5px), flag as snap candidate |
| 5 | Select the closest candidate per axis (only one snap per axis per frame) |
| 6 | If snap found: adjust element position; add guide line to `activeGuides` |
| 7 | Store renders `activeGuides` as SVG lines on `SnapGuideOverlay` |
| 8 | On pointer up: clear `activeGuides` |

### 8.3 Guide Line Rendering

| Guide Type | SVG Line | Color | Width |
|------------|----------|-------|-------|
| Vertical (element edge/center) | `<line x1=refX y1=0 x2=refX y2=canvasHeight>` | `theme.palette.primary.main` | 1px |
| Horizontal (element edge/center) | `<line x1=0 y1=refY x2=canvasWidth y2=refY>` | `theme.palette.primary.main` | 1px |

**NO hardcoded color values.** Guide color comes from `theme.palette.primary.main` via Material 3 theming. Guides are rendered in `SnapGuideOverlay` as an SVG layer at template coordinates. The `TransformComponent` wrapper's scale transform applies to the SVG automatically.

### 8.4 Canvas Bounds Snap

Independently of grid/element snap, element position is always constrained:

- `element.x >= 0`
- `element.y >= 0`
- `element.x + element.width <= canvasWidth`
- `element.y + element.height <= canvasHeight`

_No guide line rendered for bounds; element simply cannot exceed bounds._

---

## 9. Zoom & Pan Implementation (react-zoom-pan-pinch)

### 9.1 Zoom

| Operation | Trigger | Implementation |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| Zoom in | Toolbar button or `Ctrl+=` | `ref.current.zoomIn(0.1)` |
| Zoom out | Toolbar button or `Ctrl+-` | `ref.current.zoomOut(0.1)` |
| Reset to 100% | Toolbar button or `Ctrl+0` | `ref.current.resetTransform()` |
| Fit to screen | Toolbar button | `ref.current.centerView()` |
| Wheel zoom | `Ctrl+wheel` (desktop) or pinch (mobile) | Handled natively by TransformWrapper (`wheel: { step: 0.1 }`) |
| Double-click | Double-click on canvas | `doubleClick: { mode: 'zoomIn', step: 0.7 }` |
| Pinch to zoom | Two-finger pinch (mobile/touch) | Handled natively by TransformWrapper (`pinch: { step: 5 }`) |

**react-zoom-pan-pinch v4 API (per node_research/react-zoom-pan-pinch.md):**
- **NO `Controls` component** — use `useControls()` hook for imperative zoom/pan
- **NO `useTransform` hook** — use `useTransformComponent()` for reactive transform state
- **Imperative ref (`ReactZoomPanPinchRef`)**: `zoomIn`, `zoomOut`, `setTransform`, `resetTransform`, `centerView`, `zoomToElement`
- **Reactive state**: `useTransformComponent()` returns `{ scale, positionX, positionY, previousScale }`

**State sync:** `TransformWrapper`'s `onTransformed` callback writes `scale` → `zoomLevel`, `positionX/Y` → `panOffset` to the Zustand store. This keeps the store in sync with the library's internal state.

### 9.2 Pan

| Operation | Trigger | Implementation |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| Spacebar + drag | Hold Space + pointer down on canvas | Set `isPanning = true`; TransformWrapper handles pan via `panning: { disabled: false }` only when spacebar held (toggle `panning.disabled` in store) |
| Middle mouse drag | Middle button pointer down | TransformWrapper detects middle mouse natively |
| Trackpad scroll | Two-finger scroll on trackpad | TransformWrapper handles natively |
| Touch pan | Two-finger drag on touch screen | TransformWrapper handles natively |

**Pan boundaries enforced by `limitToBounds: true`** — canvas cannot be dragged outside viewport. No manual clamping needed.

### 9.3 Ruler Sync

Rulers listen to `zoomLevel` and `panOffset` from the Zustand store and update their tick mark positions accordingly:

- Horizontal ruler: `transform: translateX(-panOffset.x * zoom) scale(zoom)` on mark container
- Vertical ruler: `transform: translateY(-panOffset.y * zoom) scale(zoom)` on mark container

This ensures ruler markings align with canvas content as user pans and zooms.

---

## 10. Keyboard Shortcut Handling

### 10.1 Registration

Keyboard shortcuts are registered on a single `keydown` listener attached to `window`, but gated by `canvasFocus` state (set when canvas container receives focus, cleared on blur). This prevents shortcuts from firing when the user is typing in a text input field.

### 10.2 Shortcut Table

| Shortcut | Action | Notes |
|----------|--------|-------|
| `←` / `↑` / `→` / `↓` | Nudge selected by 1px | Updates element x/y; coalesce into single undo entry |
| `Shift+Arrow` | Nudge selected by 10px | Same, larger step |
| `Delete` / `Backspace` | Delete selected element(s) | Pushes DeleteElement command |
| `Ctrl+D` / `Cmd+D` | Duplicate selected element(s) | Pushes DuplicateElement command; new selection = duplicates |
| `Ctrl+Z` / `Cmd+Z` | Undo | Pops history, applies inverse |
| `Ctrl+Shift+Z` / `Cmd+Shift+Z` | Redo | Pops redoHistory, applies execute |
| `Ctrl+A` / `Cmd+A` | Select all elements | `selectAll()` — sets `selectedIds` to all element IDs |
| `Ctrl+C` / `Cmd+C` | Copy selected element(s) | `copySelection()` — stores serialized elements in `clipboard` |
| `Ctrl+V` / `Cmd+V` | Paste from clipboard | `paste()` — inserts clipboard elements at offset (+20px, +20px); new selection = pasted |
| `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` | Save | Triggers `saveCanvas()` — prevents default browser save dialog |
| `]` | Bring to front | `bringToFront(selectedIds)` — renormalizes zIndex |
| `[` | Send to back | `sendToBack(selectedIds)` — renormalizes zIndex |
| `Escape` | Deselect all + blur canvas | `deselectAll()` then `container.blur()` to return to document Tab order |
| `Ctrl+=` | Zoom in | `ref.current.zoomIn(0.1)` — clamped to maxScale 4.0 |
| `Ctrl+-` | Zoom out | `ref.current.zoomOut(0.1)` — clamped to minScale 0.25 |
| `Ctrl+0` | Reset zoom to 100% | `ref.current.resetTransform()` |
| `Space` (hold) | Enable pan mode | Sets `isPanning = true`; on pointer down enters `panning` state |

### 10.3 Focus Management

| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| Canvas container `onFocus` | `setCanvasFocus(true)` |
| Canvas container `onBlur` | `setCanvasFocus(false)` |
| User clicks on input within element | Element renderer calls `e.stopPropagation()` on pointer down to prevent canvas focus shift |
| User clicks anywhere outside canvas | `onBlur` fires → `setCanvasFocus(false)` → shortcuts disabled |

---

## 11. Performance Considerations

| Concern | Strategy | Implementation |
|---------|----------|----------------|
| Drag smoothness | `requestAnimationFrame` throttle on pointer move | Only apply position update on rAF tick; skip intermediate moves |
| Store re-render scope | Fine-grained selectors | `useCanvasStore(s => s.elements.find(e => e.id === myId))` — only re-renders affected `ElementRenderer` |
| Handle layer re-render | Memoized `SelectionFrame` component | `React.memo` + shallow comparison; only re-renders when `selectedIds` or specific element changes |
| SVG guide layer | Memoized `SnapGuideOverlay` | Only re-renders when `activeGuides` array reference changes (store creates new array on change) |
| Element count | 5–30 elements typical, 50 max | No virtualization needed — `React.memo` per element is sufficient. Virtualization breaks absolute positioning and hit-testing. Above 50 elements, apply `visibility: hidden` via IntersectionObserver for off-screen elements (not unmount — preserves selection state) |
| Debounced GraphQL saves | Save only on `pointerup` or explicit Save button | No automatic saves during drag; `pointerup` triggers save via Save button or Ctrl+S. Auto-save every 30s if `isDirty` (aligned with Plans 10/12 auto-save policy) |
| Large history stacks | Max 50 entries | `history.shift()` when exceeding; efficient slice or ring buffer |

### 11.1 Frame Budget Breakdown (60fps = 16.6ms)

| Phase | Budget | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Pointer event handler | 1ms | Read pointer coords, compute delta |
| Store update | 2ms | Zustand set() — immutable update of elements array |
| React re-render (only changed element) | 3ms | Memoized elements skip; only dragged element + handle overlay re-render |
| DOM commit | 2ms | CSS transform update (translate) — GPU-accelerated |
| Guide computation | 3ms | Simple O(n) scan for snap candidates |
| Total | ~11ms | < 16.6ms budget ✅ |

---

## 12. i18n Design

### 12.1 i18n Namespace

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Translation handle | `Translation.Dashboard.CertificatesCanvas` |
| Client hook | `useAppTranslation(Translation.Dashboard.CertificatesCanvas)` |
| Server-side | `getTranslations(locale).dashboardTranslations.certificatesCanvas` |
| Type file | `shared/locale/types/dashboard/certificates/canvas.ts` |
| EN namespace | `shared/locale/en/dashboard/certificates/canvas.ts` |
| AR namespace | `shared/locale/ar/dashboard/certificates/canvas.ts` |
| Registration | `shared/locale/namespaces/translation.ts` — add to `DashboardTranslations` and `Translation.Dashboard` |

**Key structure**: Nested TS object fields, NOT dot-nested strings. Define as:

```typescript
export interface CertificatesCanvasLabels {
  toolbar: { addElement: string; undo: string; ... };
  shapes: { rectangle: string; ... };
  messages: { elementDeleted: (count: number) => string; ... };
  shortcuts: { nudge: string; ... };
  properties: { content: string; fontFamily: string; ... };
  aria: { canvasRegion: string; elementText: string; ... };
}
```

