### 12.12 Arabic Pluralization Rules

For `messages.elementDeleted` / `messages.elementsDeleted` (count-based):

| Count | English | Arabic |
|-------|---------|--------|
| 1 | "Element deleted" | "تم حذف عنصر واحد" |
| 2 | "Elements deleted" | "تم حذف عنصران" |
| 3–10 | "Elements deleted" | "تم حذف {count} عناصر" |
| 11+ | "Elements deleted" | "تم حذف {count} عنصرًا" |

**Type signature in locale schema:**
`elementDeleted: (count: number) => string`

**Arabic implementation pattern:** Uses standard Arabic dual/plural rules:
- count === 1 → singular form
- count === 2 → dual form (عنصران)
- 3 ≤ count ≤ 10 → plural with {count} preceding (عناصر)
- count > 10 → singular noun with {count} preceding (عنصرًا)

### 12.13 Interpolation Pattern

Zoom level display uses interpolation:
`messages.zoomLevel: (level: number) => string`
- English: `` `Zoom: ${level}%` ``
- Arabic: `` `التكبير: ${level}%` ``

