## 17. Cross-Plan Contracts & Policies

### 17.1 Text Overflow Policy (cross-plan with Plan 6)

| Aspect | Canvas Editor (Plan 11) | PDF Renderer (Plan 6) |
|--------|-------------------------|----------------------|
| Overflow behavior | `overflow: hidden` — content clipped at bounding box edge | Must match: clip at bounding box edge |
| Visual warning | `WarningAmberOutlined` badge at top-right corner when content height exceeds bounding box | N/A — renderer has no editor UI |
| Max content length | 1000 chars (enforced in PropertyPanel `OutlinedInput` `maxLength`) | Same — Plan 6 reads element `content` as-is |
| `textOverflow` property | Not in v1 element model; clip is the only behavior | Same |

**Contract:** Plan 11 clips text at the bounding box. Plan 6's Puppeteer renderer must produce identical clipping. No `shrink-to-fit` or `ellipsis` in v1.

### 17.2 Auto-Save Policy (cross-plan with Plans 10, 12)

| Editor surface | Auto-save? | Trigger | Indicator |
|----------------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| Plan 10 — Template metadata form | Yes | 30s debounce after last field edit | "Saving…" / "Saved" in form header |
| Plan 11 — Canvas elements | **No auto-save mid-drag** | Manual: Save button or Ctrl+S. Auto-save every 30s only if `isDirty` and no active interaction (`interactionState === null`) | `isDirty` dot in toolbar; "Saving…" spinner on Save button |
| Plan 12 — Element properties form | Yes | 30s debounce after last field edit | Same as Plan 10 |

**Rationale:** Auto-saving during drag/resize is dangerous — the element is in an intermediate state. Canvas auto-save fires only when the user is idle (no active pointer interaction).

### 17.3 Element Type Model Alignment (cross-plan with Plan 12)

The `CanvasElement` discriminated union (§4.1) is the **single canonical element type model** shared across Plans 11, 12, and 15:

- Plan 11 (this plan): Canvas store uses `CanvasElement[]` for rendering + positioning
- Plan 12: Property panel reads/writes the typed branches of the same union
- Plan 15: Publish/publish-history snapshots store serialized `CanvasElement[]`
- Plan 6: Puppeteer renderer consumes `CanvasElement[]` from the published template version

**No `props: Record<string, unknown>` bag** — type-specific properties are inline in each discriminated union member.

### 17.4 DPI Convention (cross-plan with Plans 6, 10)

| Plan | DPI | Pixels for A4 (210×297mm) |
|------|-----|--------------------------|
| Plan 11 (canvas) | **96 DPI** | 794×1123 template-px |
| Plan 10 (template presets) | 96 DPI (aligned) | 794×1123 |
| Plan 6 (PDF renderer) | 96 DPI for layout; 300 DPI for raster images | 794×1123 layout grid |

**96 DPI is the canonical unit for template pixels** (per INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS §18) — both template coordinates and screen rendering use 96 DPI, eliminating the 72→96 conversion. Template data stores positions in 96 DPI template-px.

### 17.5 Permission Keys (aligned with INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS)

| Permission Key | Granted By | Plan 11 Usage |
|----------------|------------|---------------|
| `certificates.templates.manage` | `cert-templates` service | Full canvas edit: add, drag, resize, rotate, delete, save |
| `certificates.templates.view` | `cert-templates` service | Read-only canvas: view elements, zoom, toggle grid |

