## Round 5: Advanced Layers Panel

> **Scope of Round 5 in this plan**: Plan 11 owns the canvas-side rendering, visibility, and ordering behavior that backs the layers panel from Plan 10 + Plan 12. Per-row layer UI (rows, operations, groups, blending, clipping, properties) lives in Plan 12 §"Round 5: Advanced Layers Panel"; panel chrome (header, search bar, options dialog, dock state) lives in Plan 10 §"Round 5: Advanced Layers Panel". Plan 11 Round 5 covers: **layer render order on canvas**, **layer visibility on canvas**, **group composite rendering**, **clipping mask canvas rendering**, **drag-to-reorder z-index transient bump**, **scroll-sync with panel selection**, **masked/hidden layer interactions with selection & export**.
>
> This Round 5 domain is the **4th** independent Round 5 realm in this file (after Effects Engine and any prior Round 5 subsections). Sub-numbering `R5.1`, `R5.2…` restarts for this domain — this is the deliberate convention per Plan 10 Round 5 Effects Engine and Plan 12 Round 5 Fill & Stroke.

### R5.1 — Layer Rendering Order on Canvas

**Goal**: The `CanvasRenderer` already iterates `template.elements` in z-index order (R3-T06 `CanvasRenderer` + R3-T07 `CanvasLayerRenderer`). Round 5 replaces the flat z-index iteration with a **layer-tree-aware compositor** that respects groups, clipping masks, and per-layer visibility/opacity/blend-mode state.

**Data inputs** (read from `useTemplateElementEditorStore` — Plan 12 §R5 owns canonical):
- `layers`: ordered array of layer descriptors (`{ id, elementId, name, kind: 'text'|'image'|'shape'|'group', visible, locked, opacity, fillOpacity, blendMode, colorTag, maskId?, clipToBelow?: boolean, groupId?: string | null, depth: number }`)
- `groups`: ordered array of group descriptors (`{ id, name, colorTag, visible, locked, opacity, blendMode, expanded, parentId?: string | null }`)
- `layerMasks`: map `layerId → MaskDescriptor` (mask canvas, mask linked, mask enabled)
- `clipRelations`: map `layerId → baseLayerId` (clipping-mask base)

**Rendering algorithm** (`CanvasLayerCompositor` — new module):
1. Build a **flat render list** by walking the layer tree depth-first (groups first, then their children in declared order), producing `[ layer, … ]` ordered bottom-to-top (lowest z first).
2. For each layer:
   - **Skip hidden layers**: `if (!layer.visible) continue;` — also skip layers whose parent group chain has any `visible === false`.
   - **Apply group opacity**: multiply ancestor group opacities. Effective opacity = `layer.opacity * ∏ ancestorGroups.opacity`.
   - **Apply group blend mode**: if the nearest ancestor group with a non-default blend mode exists, the layer composites within the group's isolated group first, then the group composites onto its parent with the group's own blend mode.
   - **Apply clipping mask**: if `clipRelations[layerId]` is set, render the layer into an offscreen canvas clipped to the base layer's alpha shape; composite the offscreen result onto the main canvas.
   - **Apply layer mask**: if `layerMasks[layerId].enabled`, multiply the layer's alpha by the mask's luminance before compositing.
   - **Apply blend mode**: composite using the layer's `blendMode` (`source-over` default) — see Plan 12 §R5.5 Layer Blending for the 46-mode table.
3. The compositor runs on every frame **or** on demand via `requestCompositorFrame()` — debounced 16 ms so rapid slider drags don't storm.

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerCompositor.ts` (new — pure functions, no React)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/useLayerRenderOrder.ts` (new hook — wraps the compositor for React; memoized with `useMemo` keyed on `layers` + `groups` + `clipRelations` + `layerMasks`)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasRenderer.tsx` (modify R3-T06 — replace the flat `.map` with `compositor.compose(layers, groups, options)`)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerRenderer.tsx` (modify R3-T07 — accept `effectiveOpacity` and `blendMode` props from the compositor pass)

**Performance**:
- Offscreen canvas for clipping/mask composites is allocated per layer per frame; pooled via `OffscreenCanvasPool` (new module — avoids GC churn on rapid slider drags)
- For layers with no mask/clip/group effects, the compositor takes a fast path: skip offscreen, composite directly (equivalent to current R3 path)
- Layer count > 100 → compositor uses a `requestAnimationFrame`-gated render schedule (one composite per frame max, dropping intermediate updates)

### R5.2 — Layer Visibility on Canvas

**Goal**: Toggling a layer's visibility eye in the panel (Plan 12 §R5.1) must immediately remove the layer from the canvas render. Hidden layers:
- Are **not rendered** on canvas (R5.1 algorithm skips them)
- Are **not selectable** on canvas — `CanvasInteractionLayer` (R3-T09) filters out hidden layers from hit-testing
- Are **not exported** to PDF/PNG — the export pipeline (Plan 6 §PDF export) uses the same `compositor.compose()` output, so hidden layers never reach the export
- Retain their **z-index slot** — hiding a layer does NOT shift other layers' z-indices (consistency with Photoshop: hidden layer keeps its position in the stack)

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasInteractionLayer.tsx` (modify R3-T09 — filter `hitTestCandidates` to `layers.filter(l => l.visible && ancestorGroupsAllVisible(l))`)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/useLayerRenderOrder.ts` (new — see R5.1)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/export/PdfExportPipeline.ts` (verify — should already consume the composator output; if it iterates raw `template.elements` directly, refactor to call `compositor.compose()`)

**Edge case — hidden layer was selected when hidden**:
- If a layer is selected and then hidden (via eye toggle), the canvas drops the selection — `setSelectedElementIds([])` is called by the store action `setLayerVisible(id, false)` when `selectedElementIds.includes(id)`
- The PropertiesPanel auto-switches to "no selection" empty state (R4-T19)
- Undo restores both visibility AND selection

### R5.3 — Group Composite Rendering

**Goal**: Groups render as an isolated composite when they have a non-default blend mode. Otherwise, layers in a group render inline (each layer composites directly onto the canvas at its z-position).

**Algorithm**:
- If `group.blendMode === 'normal'` AND `group.opacity === 1` AND no ancestor has a non-default blend: **inline mode** — render each child directly, no offscreen buffer
- Otherwise: **isolated mode** — render all children into an offscreen canvas, then composite the offscreen result onto the parent with `group.blendMode` and `group.opacity`
- Nested groups compose recursively: innermost isolated group finishes first, then its result composites into the next outer group's offscreen buffer

**Group visibility cascade**:
- `group.visible === false` → skip the entire group subtree (R5.1 algorithm)
- `group.locked === true` → all children become non-selectable on canvas (R5.2 hit-test filter)
- Group opacity multiplication: `childEffectiveOpacity = childOpacity * groupOpacity * ∏ ancestorGroupOpacities`

**Group thumbnail** (consumed by Plan 12 §R5.3 layer row):
- Group row thumbnail = downscaled snapshot of the group's offscreen composite (40x40 default)
- Generated on-demand when group is expanded or when any child mutates; cached in `groupThumbnails: Map<groupId, string>` in the store
- Cache invalidation: bump on any child `setLayerOpacity`, `setLayerBlendMode`, `setLayerVisible`, child content mutation

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerCompositor.ts` (modify R5.1 — add `composeGroup(group, children, options)`)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/useGroupThumbnail.ts` (new hook — subscribes to group + its children, generates thumbnail via the compositor on mutation)

### R5.4 — Clipping Mask Canvas Rendering

**Goal**: When a layer is clipped to the layer below it (Alt+click between two layers — Plan 12 §R5.6), the clipped layer renders ONLY where the base layer has non-transparent pixels. The visual effect: the clipped layer's content is "shaped" by the base layer's alpha.

**Rendering**:
1. Render the base layer normally (with its own opacity/blend/mask)
2. For each clipped layer (in z-order above the base):
   - Render the clipped layer into an offscreen canvas at full opacity
   - Use `destination-in` compositing with the base layer's alpha shape to mask the offscreen canvas
   - Composite the masked offscreen canvas onto the main canvas with the clipped layer's `opacity` and `blendMode`
3. Multiple layers clipped to the same base stack: each one masks against the base's alpha (not the cumulative clipped stack) — standard Photoshop behavior

**Visual indicator on canvas** (optional): the clipped layer's bounding box renders with a dashed outline (`sx={{ borderStyle: 'dashed' }}`) when selected, to indicate the clip relationship. Toggle via `showClipIndicators` panel option (Plan 10 §R5.4).

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerCompositor.ts` (modify — add `composeClippingGroup(baseLayer, clippedLayers, options)`)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/useLayerRenderOrder.ts` (modify — group consecutive `clipToBelow` layers with their base)

### R5.5 — Drag-to-Reorder Z-Index Transient Bump

**Goal**: When the user drags a layer to a new position in the panel (Plan 12 §R5.2 drag-reorder), the canvas must immediately reflect the new z-order for visual feedback — without committing the store change until drop.

**Mechanism**:
- During drag (`@dnd-kit` `onDragStart` → `onDragEnd`), the panel calls `setTransientLayerOrder(orderedIds)` — a transient store field that the compositor consults before the canonical `layers` array
- The compositor (`useLayerRenderOrder`) reads `transientLayerOrder ?? layers.map(l => l.id)` and reorders accordingly
- On `onDragEnd`, the panel calls `commitLayerOrder()` which writes the reordered `layers` array and clears `transientLayerOrder`
- On `onDragCancel` (Escape), the panel calls `clearTransientLayerOrder()` — canvas snaps back to committed order

**Files**:
- `frontend/common/stores/certificates/templateElementEditorStore.ts` (modify — add `transientLayerOrder: string[] | null`, `setTransientLayerOrder`, `commitLayerOrder`, `clearTransientLayerOrder`; see Plan 12 §R5 store tasks for canonical ownership — Plan 11 only consumes)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/useLayerRenderOrder.ts` (modify — consult `transientLayerOrder`)

### R5.6 — Scroll-Sync with Panel Selection

**Goal**: When the user selects a layer on the canvas (click, marquee, or keyboard `Tab` cycle), the layers panel (Plan 10 §R5.3 `AdvancedLayersList`) must scroll to bring the newly-selected row into view.

**Contract** (owned by the panel, not the canvas):
- The canvas fires `setSelectedElementIds(ids)` — no special "scroll-to" signal
- The panel's `AdvancedLayersList` subscribes to `selectedElementIds` and runs the scroll-to logic (Plan 10 §R5.3 already specifies this: `scrollToIndex(idx, { align: 'center' })` with 120 ms debounce)
- Plan 11's only responsibility: ensure `selectedElementIds` updates are **synchronous** (not batched) so the panel's `useEffect` fires on the same frame. The store's `setSelectedElementIds` is already synchronous (Zustand default), so no change needed

**Edge case — marquee selection spams updates**:
- Marquee drag fires `setSelectedElementIds` on every `pointermove` that changes the hit set (R3-T09)
- The panel debounces scroll-to 120 ms; excessive `selectedElementIds` updates are fine — only the final debounce fires the scroll

**Files**: none modified in Plan 11 — verified behavior; documented here for completeness.

### R5.7 — Layer Mask Canvas Rendering

**Goal**: A layer mask (Plan 12 §R5.4 mask button) modifies the layer's alpha channel based on the mask's luminance. White mask = fully visible, black mask = fully hidden, gray = partial.

**Rendering** (in the compositor — R5.1 step):
- When `layerMasks[layerId].enabled`:
  - Render the layer normally into an offscreen canvas
  - Render the mask canvas (a separate `Canvas` the user paints on — Plan 12 §R5 owns the mask editor UI) as a grayscale image
  - Use `destination-in` compositing with the mask to multiply the layer's alpha by the mask's luminance
  - Composite the masked offscreen result onto the main canvas with the layer's `opacity` and `blendMode`
- Mask disabled → fast path: skip offscreen, composite directly

**Mask canvas storage**:
- `layerMasks: Map<layerId, MaskDescriptor>` where `MaskDescriptor = { canvasData: ImageData | string (dataURL), enabled: boolean, linked: boolean }`
- Owned by Plan 12 §R5 store; Plan 11 only reads

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerCompositor.ts` (modify — add `applyLayerMask(layer, offscreen, maskDescriptor)`)

### R5.8 — Blend Mode Canvas Compositing

**Goal**: The compositor must apply each layer's `blendMode` (Plan 12 §R5.5 — 46 modes from R5 Effects Engine) when compositing onto the canvas.

**Implementation**:
- Use the **Canvas 2D `globalCompositeOperation`** API for the subset of blend modes that map directly (25 of 46 modes: `source-over`, `multiply`, `screen`, `overlay`, `darken`, `lighten`, `color-dodge`, `color-burn`, `hard-light`, `soft-light`, `difference`, `exclusion`, `hue`, `saturation`, `color`, `luminosity`, plus `destination-in/out/atop/xor` for masking)
- For modes NOT in the Canvas 2D API (the remaining 21 — e.g., `linear-burn`, `vivid-light`, `pin-light`, `hard-mix`, `subtract`, `divide`, `grain-extract`, `grain-merge`): implement per-pixel WebGL via a `WebGLBlendPipeline` (new module) that runs a fragment shader reading the source and destination textures and applying the blend formula
- WebGL pipeline is initialized lazily on first non-Canvas2D blend mode request; cached on the canvas element
- Fallback: if WebGL unavailable, the non-Canvas2D modes degrade to `source-over` with a console warning (via `logger.warn` — NEVER `console.warn`)

**Files**:
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/CanvasLayerCompositor.ts` (modify — switch on `blendMode` between Canvas2D fast path and WebGL pipeline)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/WebGLBlendPipeline.ts` (new — WebGL2 context + fragment shaders for the 21 non-Canvas2D blend modes)
- `frontend/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/shaders/` (new directory — one `.glsl` file per non-Canvas2D blend mode for maintainability)

### R5.9 — Accessibility & Keyboard Navigation

- `CanvasRenderer` root `role="img"` with `aria-label={t("certificateEditor.canvas.label")}` — already handled in R3-T06
- Hidden layers: no `aria-hidden` needed (they're not rendered)
- Group collapse does NOT affect canvas render — groups always render their children on canvas regardless of panel collapse state (collapse is panel-only UI)
- Keyboard layer reorder (Plan 12 §R5.2 Ctrl+]/[) fires `bringForward` / `sendBackward` store actions — the canvas re-renders via the compositor; no canvas-side keyboard handler needed
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: the `Grow`/`Slide` transitions on visibility toggle are gated behind `useMediaQuery('(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)')` — when reduced motion is preferred, toggles are instant

