**Non-persisted**: Session-only (like `useCanvasStore`). Not saved to the server — guides and grid are workspace tools, not template content.

### R5-G.14 Info Bar

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/cert-canvas/components/InfoBar.tsx` (new)

A horizontal bar at the bottom of the canvas area (below the canvas viewport, above the status bar if any). Displays live contextual information:

```tsx
interface InfoBarProps {
  cursorPosition: { x: number; y: number } | null;
  selectedElement: CanvasElement | null;
  zoom: number;
  canvasSize: { width: number; height: number };
  unit: RulerUnit;
  dragInfo: DragInfo | null;        // populated during drag/resize/rotate/guide-drag
  colorMode: 'RGB' | 'CMYK';
}

interface DragInfo {
  type: 'move' | 'resize' | 'rotate' | 'guide-drag';
  delta?: { x: number; y: number };
  newDimensions?: { width: number; height: number };
  rotation?: number;
  guidePosition?: number;
}
```

**Layout** (MUI v9 `sx`):

```tsx
<Stack
  direction="row"
  spacing={2}
  sx={{
    height: 24,
    px: 1,
    backgroundColor: (theme) => theme.palette.background.paper,
    borderTop: 1,
    borderColor: (theme) => theme.palette.divider,
    alignItems: 'center',
    fontFamily: 'monospace',
    fontSize: 11,
    color: (theme) => theme.palette.text.secondary,
  }}
>
  <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11 }}>
    {t('infoBar.cursor')}: {formatPos(cursorPosition)}
  </Typography>
  {selectedElement && (
    <>
      <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11 }}>
        {t('infoBar.selection')}: {formatDim(selectedElement)}
      </Typography>
      <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11 }}>
        {t('infoBar.position')}: {formatPos({ x: selectedElement.x, y: selectedElement.y })}
      </Typography>
    </>
  )}
  <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11, ml: 'auto' }}>
    {t('infoBar.zoom')}: {(zoom * 100).toFixed(0)}%
  </Typography>
  <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11 }}>
    {t('infoBar.document')}: {canvasSize.width} × {canvasSize.height}px
  </Typography>
  <Typography component="span" sx={{ fontSize: 11 }}>
    {colorMode}
  </Typography>
  {dragInfo && <DragInfoDisplay dragInfo={dragInfo} unit={unit} />}
</Stack>
```

During drag operations, the info bar shows the delta/rotation/guide-position dynamically:

| Drag type | Info bar shows |
|---|---|
| `move` | `ΔX: 145px, ΔY: -30px` |
| `resize` | `W: 250px, H: 120px` |
| `rotate` | `∠: 45.0°` |
| `guide-drag` | `Guide Y: 397px` |

### R5-G.15 Performance Budget

- **Ruler tick computation**: `computeRulerTicks` runs in O(n) where n = canvasSize/minorInterval. With zoom-aware density, n stays under 200 ticks for any zoom level. Recomputed only on zoom/unit change (memoized).
- **Guide overlay**: O(g) where g = guide count. Guides are SVG `<line>` elements — < 200 guides is trivially fast. Guide drag uses `requestAnimationFrame` throttling.
- **Grid overlay**: `renderGrid` produces O(canvasSize / size * 2) lines. For a 794×1123 canvas with 50px grid: ~38 lines. For dot grid: ~340 dots. Memoized on config/zoom change. The SVG renders in < 2ms.
- **Smart guides**: `computeSmartGuides` is O(n) where n = other elements. For n=50, ~300 comparisons per frame. Runs at 60fps during drag with `requestAnimationFrame`.
- **Snap engine**: `applySnap` is O(priority targets) — typically 5 targets per axis. Negligible cost.
- **Info bar**: Updates at most once per `pointermove` (throttled to 60fps via rAF). The typography spans use `React.memo`.

### R5-G.16 Guide Hover Tooltip

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/cert-canvas/components/GuideTooltip.tsx` (new)

When the cursor hovers over a guide line, a small tooltip appears showing the guide's position in the current ruler unit: `"X: 500px"` or `"Y: 12.5cm"`.

Uses MUI `Tooltip` with `placement="top"` for horizontal guides and `placement="right"` for vertical guides. The tooltip is portal-rendered to avoid clipping by the canvas container.

**Performance**: Tooltip only renders for the guide under the cursor (hit-testing via `pointermove` + nearest-guide lookup). `guideGridStore.guides` is filtered for the nearest guide within 5px of cursor.


## Round 5: Custom Shapes & Boolean Operations

> Added as Round 5. Extends the canvas with production-grade shape rendering, drawing interactions, shape edit mode (anchor-point editing), boolean operation path math, shape caching, and hit detection. This plan covers the **canvas rendering and interaction** portions; the toolbar/panel UI is in Plan 10 and property controls are in Plan 12.

### R5.1 Shape Element Type & Rendering

**Component**: `ShapeNode`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/nodes/ShapeNode.tsx`

**Design**:

Shape elements render as SVG elements within the React Flow node. The specific SVG element type depends on `shapeType`:

```typescript
type ShapeType =
  | 'rectangle'
  | 'roundedRectangle'
  | 'ellipse'
  | 'polygon'
  | 'star'
  | 'triangle'
  | 'line'
  | 'custom'
  | 'boolean';
```

```typescript
interface ShapeElementData extends CertNodeData {
  shapeType: ShapeType;
  // Geometry
  width: number;
  height: number;
  rotation: number;          // degrees, -180 to +180
  // Type-specific
  cornerRadius?: CornerRadiusConfig;     // rectangle, roundedRectangle
  polygonSides?: number;                   // polygon: 3–12
  starPoints?: number;                     // star: 3–20
  starInnerRadius?: number;                // star: inner radius as % of outer (10–90)
  triangleType?: 'equilateral' | 'isosceles' | 'scalene';
  triangleDirection?: 'up' | 'down' | 'left' | 'right';
  lineThickness?: number;                  // line: 1–20px
  lineStyle?: 'solid' | 'dashed' | 'dotted';
  lineArrowStart?: 'none' | 'solid' | 'open' | 'triangle';
  lineArrowEnd?: 'none' | 'solid' | 'open' | 'triangle';
  ellipseStartAngle?: number;              // ellipse: 0–360 for arc/pie
  ellipseEndAngle?: number;                // ellipse: 0–360
  pathData?: string;                        // custom: SVG path d attribute
  // Boolean
  booleanConfig?: BooleanConfig;
  // Fill & stroke: from R5-fill-stroke system (Round 4)
  fill?: FillConfig;
  stroke?: StrokeConfig;
}
```

```typescript
interface CornerRadiusConfig {
  uniform: boolean;
  all: number;                          // used when uniform=true
  topLeft: number;
  topRight: number;
  bottomLeft: number;
  bottomRight: number;
}

interface BooleanConfig {
  operation: BooleanOperation;
  operandIds: string[];
  operands: ShapeOperand[];
}

interface ShapeOperand {
  elementId: string;
  pathData: string;
  transform: { x: number; y: number; rotation: number; scaleX: number; scaleY: number };
}
```

#### R5.1.1 SVG Rendering by Shape Type

The `ShapeNode` component renders an inline `<svg>` with a single shape child element:

**Rectangle** → `<rect>`:
```tsx
<rect
  width={data.width}
  height={data.height}
  rx={data.cornerRadius?.uniform ? data.cornerRadius.all : 0}
  ry={data.cornerRadius?.uniform ? data.cornerRadius.all : 0}
  fill={fillColor}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  strokeWidth={strokeWidth}
/>
```

**Rounded Rectangle** (per-corner radius) → `<path>` (SVG `<rect>` doesn't support per-corner radius, so we generate path data):
```tsx
// Path generation for per-corner rounded rectangle
const d = generateRoundedRectPath(
  0, 0, data.width, data.height,
  data.cornerRadius.uniform
    ? { tl: data.cornerRadius.all, tr: data.cornerRadius.all, bl: data.cornerRadius.all, br: data.cornerRadius.all }
    : { tl: data.cornerRadius.topLeft, tr: data.cornerRadius.topRight, bl: data.cornerRadius.bottomLeft, br: data.cornerRadius.bottomRight }
);
<path d={d} fill={fillColor} stroke={strokeColor} strokeWidth={strokeWidth} />
```

**Ellipse** → `<ellipse>` (or arcs via `<path>` when start/end angles are set):
```tsx
{!hasArc ? (
  <ellipse cx={data.width / 2} cy={data.height / 2} rx={data.width / 2} ry={data.height / 2}
    fill={fillColor} stroke={strokeColor} strokeWidth={strokeWidth} />
) : (
  <path d={generateArcPath(data.width, data.height, data.ellipseStartAngle!, data.ellipseEndAngle!)}
    fill={fillColor} stroke={strokeColor} strokeWidth={strokeWidth} />
)}
```

**Polygon** → `<polygon>`:
```tsx
<polygon
  points={generatePolygonPoints(data.width, data.height, data.polygonSides!, data.rotation)}
  fill={fillColor}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  strokeWidth={strokeWidth}
/>
```

**Star** → `<path>`:
```tsx
<path
  d={generateStarPath(data.width, data.height, data.starPoints!, data.starInnerRadius!)}
  fill={fillColor}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  strokeWidth={strokeWidth}
/>
```

**Triangle** → `<path>`:
```tsx
<path
  d={generateTrianglePath(data.width, data.height, data.triangleType!, data.triangleDirection!)}
  fill={fillColor}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  strokeWidth={strokeWidth}
/>
```

**Line** → `<line>`:
```tsx
<line
  x1={0} y1={0} x2={data.width} y2={0}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  strokeWidth={data.lineThickness}
  strokeDasharray={data.lineStyle === 'dashed' ? '8,4' : data.lineStyle === 'dotted' ? '2,2' : undefined}
  markerStart={lineArrowStart ? `url(#arrow-start-${elementId})` : undefined}
  markerEnd={lineArrowEnd ? `url(#arrow-end-${elementId})` : undefined}
/>
```

Arrow head markers are defined in `<defs>` within the same `<svg>` — small `<marker>` elements for each arrow style (solid, open, triangle).

**Custom** → `<path>`:
```tsx
<path d={data.pathData} fill={fillColor} stroke={strokeColor} strokeWidth={strokeWidth} />
```

**Boolean** → `<path>` (computed from boolean operation — see R5.4):
```tsx
<path d={booleanPathData} fill={fillColor} stroke={strokeColor} strokeWidth={strokeWidth} />
```

#### R5.1.2 Path Generation Utilities

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/utils/shapePathGenerators.ts`

Pure functions that generate SVG path data for each shape type:

```typescript
// Per-corner rounded rectangle path
export function generateRoundedRectPath(
  x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number,
  radii: { tl: number; tr: number; bl: number; br: number },
): string;

// Regular polygon points (returns "x1,y1 x2,y2 ..." for <polygon>)
export function generatePolygonPoints(
  w: number, h: number, sides: number, rotation: number,
): string;

// Star path (alternating outer/inner radius points)
export function generateStarPath(
  w: number, h: number, points: number, innerRadiusPercent: number,
): string;

// Triangle path (equilateral, isosceles, scalene; direction: up/down/left/right)
export function generateTrianglePath(
  w: number, h: number, type: 'equilateral' | 'isosceles' | 'scalene',
  direction: 'up' | 'down' | 'left' | 'right',
): string;

// Ellipse arc/pie path (for partial ellipse shapes)
export function generateArcPath(
  w: number, h: number, startAngle: number, endAngle: number,
): string;
```

#### R5.1.3 Shape Hover & Selection

**Hover**: On mouse enter, shape outline highlights using `theme.palette.primary.main` at 50% opacity (stroke overlay). The SVG element gets a CSS class `shape-hover` with:
```css
.shape-hover { stroke: var(--hover-color); stroke-width: 2; stroke-opacity: 0.5; }
```

The CSS variable is set via the `sx` prop on the wrapper:
```tsx
<Box
  sx={{
    '--hover-color': (theme) => theme.palette.primary.main,
  }}
>
```

**Selection**: Selection frame matches the shape's **bounding box** (the element's width/height), not the shape's actual outline. This uses the existing React Flow selection frame. No custom selection overlay needed — the standard `SelectedNodeWrapper` from R1 applies.

**Hit detection**: SVG elements use `pointer-events: fill` for filled shapes (click anywhere inside the shape outline selects) and `pointer-events: stroke` for outlined-only shapes (fill="none"). This is set via the `pointerEvents` CSS property on the SVG child:
```tsx
<path
  d={pathData}
  fill={fillEnabled ? fillColor : 'none'}
  stroke={strokeColor}
  style={{ pointerEvents: fillEnabled ? 'fill' : 'stroke' }}
/>
```

### R5.2 Shape Drawing Interaction

**Component**: `useShapeDrawing` (custom hook)

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/hooks/useShapeDrawing.ts`

**Design**:

When `activeShapeTool` is not `'select'`, the canvas enters drawing mode. The hook attaches `onMouseDown`, `onMouseMove`, `onMouseUp` handlers to the canvas background element (React Flow's `panOnDrag` is disabled during draw mode).

**Drawing flow**:
1. `onMouseDown` on canvas background → records start point `{ x, y }` in canvas coordinates. Creates a "preview" shape element with initial `{ width: 0, height: 0 }` at start point.
2. `onMouseMove` → updates preview shape's width/height based on current pointer position relative to start point. If `Shift` is held, constrains to proportional (max(|dx|, |dy|) for both). If `Alt` is held, adjusts position so the shape is centered on the start point (draw from center).
3. `onMouseUp` → finalizes the shape element. If width and height are both < 2px (accidental click), the preview is discarded (no shape created). Otherwise, the shape element is added to the store as a permanent canvas element. Drawing mode stays active (user can draw another shape). `Esc` or `V` key returns to select mode.

**Proportional constraint** (Shift key):
```typescript
if (e.shiftKey) {
  const maxDim = Math.max(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));
  width = maxDim;
  height = shapeType === 'line' ? 0 : maxDim;
}
```

Special proportional rules per shape type:
- Rectangle → square (width = height)
- Rounded Rectangle → square (width = height)
- Ellipse → circle (width = height)
- Polygon → equilateral (width = height, rotation adjusted for orientation)
- Star → uniform (width = height)
- Triangle → equilateral (width = height)
- Line → horizontal (height = 0, width = drag distance)
- Custom → free-form (Shift has no effect on custom shapes from library)

**Draw from center** (Alt key):
```typescript
if (e.altKey) {
  // Start point is the center; shape extends in all directions
  x = startPoint.x - width / 2;
  y = startPoint.y - height / 2;
} else {
  // Start point is the top-left corner
  x = startPoint.x;
  y = startPoint.y;
  // Handle negative drag (drag up/left)
  if (dx < 0) x = startPoint.x + dx;
  if (dy < 0) y = startPoint.y + dy;
}
```

**Custom shape placement**: When `activeShapeTool === 'custom'`, the behavior differs:
- Single click → places the selected custom shape at default size centered at click point
- Click+drag → places the custom shape scaled to fit the drag rectangle (maintaining aspect ratio)

**Preview rendering**: The preview shape uses `theme.palette.primary.main` as stroke with `0.3` opacity and no fill, so the user sees a ghost outline while dragging. The preview is rendered as a React Flow node with `selected: false` and a special `isPreview: true` flag that prevents it from being saveable.

### R5.3 Shape Edit Mode (Anchor Points)

**Component**: `ShapeEditMode`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/nodes/ShapeEditMode.tsx`

**Design**:

Double-clicking a shape element (when not in drawing mode) enters **shape edit mode** — the shape displays its anchor points (vertices) as draggable handles, similar to Photoshop's Direct Selection Tool.

```tsx
interface ShapeEditModeProps {
  elementId: string;
  pathData: string;     // current SVG path data
  onPathChange: (pathData: string) => void;
  onExit: () => void;
}
```

**Anchor point rendering**: Anchor points are rendered as small circles (6px) at each path coordinate. The selected anchor point shows its Bezier control handles (direction lines) if the segment is curved.

```tsx
{anchorPoints.map((point, index) => (
  <circle
    key={index}
    cx={point.x}
    cy={point.y}
    r={3}
    fill={selectedAnchorIndex === index ? theme.palette.primary.main : theme.palette.common.white}
    stroke={theme.palette.primary.main}
    strokeWidth={1.5}
    style={{ cursor: 'move' }}
    onPointerDown={(e) => startDragAnchor(index, e)}
  />
))}
```

**Bezier handles**: For curved segments (path commands with control points like `C`, `Q`), the anchor point renders two direction handle lines extending to the Bezier control point positions. The control handle endpoints are also draggable circles:

```tsx
{selectedAnchor && selectedAnchor.hasHandles && (
  <>
    <line x1={selectedAnchor.x} y1={selectedAnchor.y} x2={selectedAnchor.handleIn.x} y2={selectedAnchor.handleIn.y}
      stroke={theme.palette.primary.main} strokeWidth={1} strokeOpacity={0.5} />
    <line x1={selectedAnchor.x} y1={selectedAnchor.y} x2={selectedAnchor.handleOut.x} y2={selectedAnchor.handleOut.y}
      stroke={theme.palette.primary.main} strokeWidth={1} strokeOpacity={0.5} />
    <circle cx={selectedAnchor.handleIn.x} cy={selectedAnchor.handleIn.y} r={2.5} fill={theme.palette.primary.light} />
    <circle cx={selectedAnchor.handleOut.x} cy={selectedAnchor.handleOut.y} r={2.5} fill={theme.palette.primary.light} />
  </>
))}
```

**Anchor operations**:
- **Drag anchor**: Pointer down → move → updates path coordinate → re-renders shape
- **Add anchor**: Click on path segment → inserts new anchor point at click position (subdivides the segment)
- **Delete anchor**: Select anchor → `Delete` key → removes point, path re-connects adjacent anchors
- **Convert anchor**: Alt+click sharp anchor → converts to smooth (adds Bezier handles); Alt+click smooth anchor → converts to sharp (removes handles)
- **Exit**: Click outside shape, `Esc` key, or double-click → exits shape edit mode, commits path

**Path parsing**: Anchor points are extracted from SVG path data using a path parser (`parsePathData(pathData)`) that returns an array of `PathCommand` objects:
```typescript
interface PathCommand {
  command: 'M' | 'L' | 'C' | 'Q' | 'A' | 'Z';
  points: { x: number; y: number }[];  // command-specific points
  handles?: { in: { x: number; y: number }; out: { x: number; y: number } }; // for C/Q commands
}
```

```typescript
export function parsePathData(d: string): PathCommand[];
export function serializePathData(commands: PathCommand[]): string;
export function insertAnchor(commands: PathCommand[], segmentIndex: number, t: number): PathCommand[];
export function deleteAnchor(commands: PathCommand[], anchorIndex: number): PathCommand[];
export function moveAnchor(commands: PathCommand[], anchorIndex: number, x: number, y: number): PathCommand[];
export function convertAnchorType(commands: PathCommand[], anchorIndex: number, toSmooth: boolean): PathCommand[];
```

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/utils/pathParser.ts` — pure path data parsing and manipulation utilities.

### R5.4 Boolean Operation Path Math

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/utils/booleanPathMath.ts`

**Design**:

Boolean operations on shapes require computing the combined path geometry from two or more input paths. This is done via the **Clipper.js** library (or a pure-JS clipper port), which handles all seven boolean operations on SVG paths.

**Dependencies**: `js-clipper` (pure JavaScript port of Angus Johnson's Clipper library) — lightweight, no native dependencies. Alternatively, `paper-js` can be used for more advanced path operations. The choice is deferred to implementation; the interface remains the same.

```typescript
import { Clipper, ClipType, PolyType, FillType } from 'js-clipper';

export function computeBooleanPath(
  operands: ShapeOperand[],
  operation: BooleanOperation,
): string {
  // 1. Convert each operand's path data to Clipper polygon format
  // 2. Apply the clip operation based on `operation`
  // 3. Convert the result back to SVG path data
}
```

**Operation implementations**:

```typescript
const CLIP_TYPE_MAP: Record<BooleanOperation, ClipType> = {
  unite:    ClipType.ctUnion,
  subtract: ClipType.ctDifference,
  intersect: ClipType.ctIntersection,
  exclude:  ClipType.ctXor,
  divide:   ClipType.ctUnion, // then split at intersections
  trim:      ClipType.ctUnion, // then cut at intersections
  merge:     ClipType.ctUnion, // compound path (no actual boolean)
};
```

**Divide**: After computing the union, the result is split into separate path segments wherever shapes intersect. Each piece becomes a separate `<path>` element with its own `pathData`. The `ShapeElementData` for a divide result stores an array of `pathData` strings:

```typescript
interface DivideResult {
  pieces: { pathData: string }[];
}
```

**Trim**: Similar to Divide, but the pieces remain as separate `ShapeElementData` elements on the canvas (not a single compound element). The original shapes are replaced by the trimmed pieces.

**Merge (compound path)**: Creates a single `<path>` with multiple subpaths (using `M` commands for each subpath). This is a **non-destructive** operation — the original operand shapes are preserved in `booleanConfig.operands` and can be re-edited by changing the operation type or flattening.

**Caching**: Boolean path computation is expensive. The result is cached in the element's `booleanConfig` as a `computedPathData` field. The cache is invalidated when any operand's path data or transform changes (tracked via a `cacheVersion` counter that increments on operand edits).

```typescript
interface BooleanConfig {
  operation: BooleanOperation;
  operandIds: string[];
  operands: ShapeOperand[];
  computedPathData?: string;    // cached result
  cacheVersion: number;          // incremented when operands change
}
```

**Flatten**: Converts the non-destructive boolean result to a single baked shape:
```typescript
export function flattenBoolean(
  element: BooleanResultElement,
  computedPath: string,
): BakedShapeElement {
  return {
    ...element,
    shapeType: 'custom',
    pathData: computedPath,
    booleanConfig: undefined,  // remove boolean config
  };
}
```

### R5.5 Shape Caching & Performance

**Component**: `ShapePathCache`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/utils/shapePathCache.ts`

**Design**:

Shape path generation (especially polygon, star, and boolean operations) is CPU-intensive and must be cached during drag interactions. The cache is a simple `Map<string, string>` keyed by a serialized representation of the shape's geometry:

```typescript
const pathCache = new Map<string, string>();

function getCacheKey(data: ShapeElementData): string {
  return JSON.stringify({
    shapeType: data.shapeType,
    width: data.width,
    height: data.height,
    rotation: data.rotation,
    cornerRadius: data.cornerRadius,
    polygonSides: data.polygonSides,
    starPoints: data.starPoints,
    starInnerRadius: data.starInnerRadius,
    triangleType: data.triangleType,
    triangleDirection: data.triangleDirection,
    pathData: data.pathData,
    booleanCacheVersion: data.booleanConfig?.cacheVersion,
  });
}

export function getCachedShapePath(data: ShapeElementData): string {
  const key = getCacheKey(data);
  if (pathCache.has(key)) return pathCache.get(key)!;
  const path = generateShapePath(data);  // compute path
  pathCache.set(key, path);
  // Evict if cache too large (LRU)
  if (pathCache.size > 500) {
    const firstKey = pathCache.keys().next().value;
    pathCache.delete(firstKey);
  }
  return path;
}
```

During drag (resize, move), shapes use the cached path for rendering. The cache is invalidated when the geometry inputs change (new key means new entry — old keys naturally age out via LRU eviction).

### R5.6 Interactive Corner Radius Handle

**Component**: `CornerRadiusHandle`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/nodes/CornerRadiusHandle.tsx`

**Design**:

When a rectangle or rounded rectangle shape is selected, an interactive corner radius handle appears at the top-left corner. Dragging this handle adjusts the corner radius in real-time.

```tsx
// The handle is a small circle positioned at the top-left corner radius center
<circle
  cx={radius}
  cy={radius}
  r={4}
  fill={theme.palette.common.white}
  stroke={theme.palette.primary.main}
  strokeWidth={1.5}
  style={{ cursor: 'ew-resize' }}
  onPointerDown={startRadiusDrag}
/>
```

**Drag logic**: The horizontal mouse distance from the corner determines the radius value. Clamped to `0` and `min(width, height) / 2`. Updates `cornerRadius.all` (for uniform mode) or `cornerRadius.topLeft` (for per-corner mode).

### R5.7 Shape Sides & Star Points Interactive Editing

**Component**: `ShapeSidesHandle`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/nodes/ShapeSidesHandle.tsx`

**Design**:

For polygon and star shapes, small `+`/`−` buttons appear near the shape when selected, allowing the user to increment/decrement sides/points without going to the property panel. These are rendered as React Flow `Handle`-adjacent overlays:

```tsx
{selected && isPolygon && (
  <Box sx={{ position: 'absolute', top: -30, left: '50%', transform: 'translateX(-50%)', display: 'flex', gap: 0.5 }}>
    <IconButton size="small" onClick={() => updatePolygonSides(Math.max(3, sides - 1))}>
      <RemoveOutlined sx={{ fontSize: 16 }} />
    </IconButton>
    <Typography sx={{ fontSize: 12, alignSelf: 'center', minWidth: 20, textAlign: 'center' }}>
      {sides}
    </Typography>
    <IconButton size="small" onClick={() => updatePolygonSides(Math.min(12, sides + 1))}>
      <AddOutlined sx={{ fontSize: 16 }} />
    </IconButton>
  </Box>
)}
```

For star shapes, additionally an inner radius handle (a small dot on the inner radius circle) can be dragged to adjust `starInnerRadius` interactively.

### R5.8 Error States for Shapes

#### R5.8.1 Invalid Path Data

When a custom or boolean shape has corrupted/invalid `pathData`:
- The `CertificateNodeErrorBoundary` (from R4) catches the render error.
- Fallback: renders a placeholder rectangle with `theme.palette.error.main` border and "Invalid shape path" text.
- A "Reset shape" button calls `updateNode(id, { shapeType: 'rectangle', pathData: undefined, width: 100, height: 100 })`.

#### R5.8.2 Boolean Operation Failure

If `computeBooleanPath` throws (degenerate paths, self-intersecting loops, precision errors):
- The boolean result element renders the **first operand** as fallback (with `theme.palette.warning.main` outline).
- A toast notification appears: "Boolean operation failed — showing original shape. Try adjusting the shapes or flattening."
- The error is logged via `logger.warn` with the operand IDs and operation type.

#### R5.8.3 SVG Import Parse Failure

If `parseSvgToShapePreset` encounters malformed SVG:
- Throws `InvalidSvgError` which is caught by the import dialog.
- The dialog displays the error message with the file name.
- No shape preset is created.

### R5.9 Store Contract for Round 5 (Canvas)

Additions to `frontend/common/stores/canvasStore.ts`:

```typescript
// Drawing mode
isDrawingShape: boolean;
drawingPreview: ShapeElementData | null;
drawingStartPoint: { x: number; y: number } | null;
startShapeDrawing: (tool: ShapeTool, start: { x: number; y: number }) => void;
updateShapeDrawing: (current: { x: number; y: number }, modifiers: { shift: boolean; alt: boolean }) => void;
endShapeDrawing: () => void;        // commits preview to permanent element
cancelShapeDrawing: () => void;       // discards preview

// Shape edit mode
editingShapeId: string | null;        // element currently in edit mode
enterShapeEditMode: (elementId: string) => void;
exitShapeEditMode: () => void;
updateShapePath: (elementId: string, pathData: string) => void;

// Boolean rendering cache
booleanPathCache: Map<string, string>;
invalidateBooleanCache: (elementId: string) => void;
```

## Round 5: Advanced Typography Engine

Round 5 in Plan 11 owns **text rendering fidelity on canvas**, **text-on-path rendering**, **text measurement**, **text caching**, **auto-fit**, **text overflow handling**, and **inline edit mode entry/exit**. The canvas must produce WYSIWYG output that matches the exported PDF pixel-for-pixel. All text rendering components live under `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/`.

### R5.1 Text Rendering Fidelity

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/TextRenderer.tsx`

The canvas text renderer wraps `RichTextRenderer` (from Plan 10) with canvas-specific concerns: DPI scaling, crisp rendering, and PDF parity.

**Rendering properties applied at the container level:**
```tsx
sx={{
  textRendering: "optimizeLegibility",
  WebkitFontSmoothing: "antialiased",
  MozOsxFontSmoothing: "grayscale",
  fontFeatureSettings: '"kern" 1, "liga" 1, "calt" 1, "rlig" 1',
}}
```

**WYSIWYG guarantee:**
- The canvas renders at the template's native resolution (e.g., 1123×794 for A4 landscape at 96 DPI).
- The PDF renderer (Plan 06) uses the same `font-family`, `font-size`, `letter-spacing`, `line-height`, `text-decoration`, `text-transform`, `text-shadow`, and `font-variation-settings` values.
- A visual diff test (`test/ui/components/canvas/textPdfParity.test.tsx`) renders the same `RichTextContent` on canvas and in a mock PDF page, comparing bounding boxes for each text run. Tolerance: ±1px per run.

**Arabic shaping:**
- The renderer sets `direction: "rtl"` and `unicode-bidi: "plaintext"` when the text content contains >50% Arabic characters (detected via Unicode range `[\u0600-\u06FF\u0750-\u077F\u08A0-\u08FF\uFB50-\uFDFF\uFE70-\uFEFF]`).
- Arabic ligatures and shaping are handled by the browser's text shaping engine (HarfBuzz in Chromium).
- `font-feature-settings: '"rlig" 1'` ensures required Arabic ligatures are applied.
- Mixed Arabic + Latin: `unicode-bidi: "plaintext"` handles per-paragraph direction detection. Baseline alignment between scripts is the browser's responsibility (both scripts share the same `line-height` and `vertical-align`).

### R5.2 Text Overflow Handling

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/useTextOverflow.ts`

Each text element has an `overflow` property in the store:

```ts
type TextOverflowMode = "truncate" | "shrink" | "clip" | "expand";

interface TextOverflowSettings {
  mode: TextOverflowMode;
  // For "truncate"
  ellipsis: boolean;        // show "…" → default true
  maxLines: number | null;  // null = unlimited
  // For "shrink"
  minFontSize: number;       // default 4px — auto-fit floor
  // For "clip"
  clipMode: "visible" | "hidden";  // "hidden" = overflow: hidden
  // For "expand"
  expandDirection: "width" | "height" | "both";  // which bound grows
}
```

**Modes:**

| Mode | Behavior | CSS / Logic |
|------|----------|-------------|
| `truncate` | Add ellipsis when text exceeds bounds | `text-overflow: ellipsis; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap;` (single-line) or multi-line truncation via line clamping (count lines with `maxLines`, if exceeded add "…") |
| `shrink` | Auto-fit: reduce font size until text fits | Binary search font size between current size and `minFontSize`. Measure text height via `CanvasRenderingContext2D.measureText`. Stop when height ≤ element height. |
| `clip` | Clip at bounds, no ellipsis | `overflow: hidden` on container |
| `expand` | Expand bounds to fit | `height: auto; width: auto` — element bounding box grows. If `expandDirection` is "width", only grow width; if "height", only grow height |

**Auto-fit algorithm (for `shrink` mode):**

```ts
function autoFitFontSize(
  text: string,
  maxWidth: number,
  maxHeight: number,
  fontFamily: string,
  fontWeight: number,
  startSize: number,
  minSize: number,
  lineHeight: number
): number {
  const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
  const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d")!;
  let size = startSize;
  const step = 0.5; // 0.5px granularity

  while (size >= minSize) {
    ctx.font = `${fontWeight} ${size}px ${fontFamily}`;
    const lines = wrapText(ctx, text, maxWidth);
    const totalHeight = lines.length * size * lineHeight;
    if (totalHeight <= maxHeight && lines.every(l => ctx.measureText(l).width <= maxWidth)) {
      return size;
    }
    size -= step;
  }
  return minSize;  // could not fit — return floor
}
```

The auto-fit runs on initial render and whenever text content, element bounds, or `RichTextContent` changes. The result is cached in `TypographyState.autoFitCache: Record<string, number>` keyed by `elementId + textContentHash`.

### R5.3 Text Measurement

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/useTextMeasurement.ts`

Real-time text width/height calculation for alignment guides, smart snapping, and overflow detection.

```ts
interface TextMeasurement {
  width: number;      // total rendered width in px
  height: number;     // total rendered height in px
  lineHeight: number;  // effective line height (fontSize * leading)
  lineCount: number;  // number of wrapped lines
  lineWidths: number[]; // width of each line
  baselineY: number;  // y position of baseline (for path text)
}

function measureText(
  content: RichTextContent,
  baseStyles: SpanStyles,
  maxWidth: number,
  padding: { top: number; right: number; bottom: number; left: number }
): TextMeasurement {
  // Uses OffscreenCanvas (if available) or a hidden canvas element
  // For mixed spans, measures the widest span in each line
  // For wrapped text, simulates word wrapping and measures each line
}
```

**Performance:** Uses `OffscreenCanvas` (Chromium) with fallback to a hidden `<canvas>` element. Measurements are cached per `elementId + contentHash + maxWidth`. Cache invalidates on any property change.

**Usage:**
- **Alignment guides** (Plan 11 §8 snap algorithms): uses `TextMeasurement.width` for center/right snapping of text elements.
- **Smart resize**: when resizing a text element, shows a measurement tooltip ("W: 240px, H: 80px, 3 lines") near the resize handle.
- **Overflow indicator**: if measured height > element height (in `truncate` mode), shows a warning badge `Icon=` (`WarningOutlined`) at the element's bottom-right corner.

### R5.4 Text Hit Area

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/TextHitArea.tsx`

The click target for text elements must match the rendered text bounds — not just the element's container bounds.

**Implementation:**
- For non-wrapped text (single line): hit area = `TextMeasurement.width × TextMeasurement.height`.
- For wrapped text: hit area = element content box (since text fills the width). Any click within the content box selects the element.
- For text-on-path: hit area = the bounding box of all glyph positions (computed during path text layout).

**Tolerance:** Clicks within 4px of the text's visible bounds count as hits (to account for descenders below baseline). This avoids the "can't click text because it has a descender sticking out" problem.

```tsx
function TextHitArea({ element, onSelect }: TextHitAreaProps) {
  const measurement = useTextMeasurement(element);
  const hitWidth = Math.max(measurement.width, element.width);
  const hitHeight = Math.max(measurement.height, element.height);
  return (
    <Box
      sx={{ position: "absolute", width: hitWidth, height: hitHeight, cursor: "pointer" }}
      onClick={() => onSelect(element.id)}
    />
  );
}
```

### R5.5 Text Caching

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/useTextCache.ts`

Renders text to an offscreen canvas and caches the bitmap for reuse during drag/pan operations.

**Cache structure:**
```ts
interface TextCacheEntry {
  bitmap: ImageBitmap | HTMLCanvasElement;
  width: number;
  height: number;
  timestamp: number;
  contentHash: string;  // hash of RichTextContent + SpanStyles + element bounds
}

// In typographyStore or a dedicated cache:
const textCache: Map<string, TextCacheEntry> = new Map();
```

**Cache invalidation:**
- Key: `elementId + contentHash`
- `contentHash` = JSON hash of `RichTextContent`, base `SpanStyles`, and element `width × height`
- Invalidates when any of: text content changes, font size/weight/style changes, element bounds change, overflow mode changes.

**Rendering during drag:**
- **Normal mode**: renders HTML spans via `RichTextRenderer` (full fidelity).
- **Drag/pan mode** (`performanceLevel: "low"`): renders the cached `ImageBitmap` instead of re-rendering spans. Toggle via `performanceConfig.textSimplifyDuringDrag` (default `true`).
- After drag ends, switches back to full HTML rendering and re-renders the cache.

**Cache eviction:**
- LRU with max 50 entries (≈ 50 text elements).
- Eviction check on cache write. Oldest entries are freed (`ImageBitmap.close()` if available).

**Cache for editor open:** On editor open, all text elements are rendered to cache immediately (in a `requestIdleCallback`) so the first drag is smooth.

### R5.6 Text Preview During Drag

When `performanceConfig.textSimplifyDuringDrag` is `true` (default):
- During drag, pan, or zoom: each text element renders as a simplified bounding box with the text color as background tint (20% opacity) and the first ~20 characters of text as a preview label.
- This prevents layout thrashing from DOM text mutations during continuous drag.
- Toggle: `Ctrl+Shift+H` toggles simplified text mode globally (keyboard shortcut registered in ShortcutManager from R4).

**Simplified rendering:**

```tsx
function SimplifiedTextPreview({ element }: { element: TextElement }) {
  const preview = element.richTextContent.text.slice(0, 20);
  return (
    <Box
      sx={{
        width: element.width,
        height: element.height,
        backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.text.primary, 0.08),
        display: "flex",
        alignItems: "center",
        justifyContent: "center",
        overflow: "hidden",
      }}
    >
      <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ color: "text.disabled" }}>
        {preview}
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

### R5.7 Text Editing (Inline Edit Mode)

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/useInlineEditMode.ts`

Custom hook managing the transition from display mode to edit mode for text elements.

**State machine:**

| Event | Current State | New State | Action |
|-------|--------------|-----------|--------|
| Double-click text element | `display` | `editing` | `typographyStore.enterEditMode(elementId)`, focus `contentEditable` |
| Escape key | `editing` | `display` | `typographyStore.exitEditMode()`, blur, commit to store |
| Click outside element | `editing` | `display` | `typographyStore.exitEditMode()`, commit |
| Tab key | `editing` | `editing` | Insert tab character (does NOT exit edit mode) |
| `Ctrl/Cmd+Enter` | `editing` | `display` | Commit + exit edit mode |

**Double-click detection:**
- React Flow's `onNodeDoubleClick` event → enters edit mode.
- On mobile: double-tap within 350ms → enters edit mode.
- Only text elements support edit mode; shape/image/QR elements ignore double-click for editing.

**Edit mode visual changes:**
- Element selection outline changes from solid to dashed (`borderStyle: "dashed"`).
- A subtle inner glow (`boxShadow: inset 0 0 0 2px ${theme.palette.primary.main}`) indicates edit mode.
- All other elements dim to 60% opacity (via canvas overlay, not per-element — performance).
- The `RichTextToolbar` appears above the element.
- The text `contentEditable` element receives focus with the caret at the click position.

**Caret positioning:**
- On entering edit mode via double-click: caret placed at the character closest to the click position (computed via `document.caretPositionFromPoint(x, y)` or `document.caretRangeFromPoint(x, y)` fallback).
- On entering edit mode via keyboard (Enter on selected text element): caret at start of text, full text selected.

**Arrow keys in edit mode:**
- Left/Right: move caret by one character (or one word with Ctrl+Left/Right).
- Up/Down: move caret by one line (simulated — move to closest line boundary).
- Shift+Arrow: extend/reduce selection.
- Ctrl+A: select all text in element.
- Ctrl+Home/End: caret to start/end of text.

### R5.8 Text Placeholder

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/TextPlaceholder.tsx`

When a text element has empty content (`text === ""` and `spans.length === 0`), show placeholder text.

```tsx
function TextPlaceholder({ element }: { element: TextElement }) {
  const { t } = useAppTranslation("certificateEditor");
  if (element.richTextContent.text.trim() !== "" || element.richTextContent.spans.length > 0) {
    return null;
  }
  return (
    <Typography
      variant="bodyMd"
      sx={{
        color: (theme) => theme.palette.text.disabled,
        fontStyle: "italic",
        pointerEvents: "none",
        userSelect: "none",
      }}
    >
      {t.typography.placeholder.empty}
    </Typography>
  );
}
```

**Placeholder text** (i18n):
- `typography.placeholder.empty` → EN: "Double-click to edit", AR: "انقر مرتين للتعديل"

### R5.9 Text on Path

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/TextOnPath.tsx`

Renders text following a vector bezier path. This enables curved text on certificates (e.g., arched text at the top of a certificate).

**Path definition:**

```ts
interface TextPath {
  id: string;
  // Cubic bezier path segments
  segments: BezierSegment[];
  // Closed path (for circular/arched text)
  closed: boolean;
  // Text direction along the path
  direction: "forward" | "reverse";
  // Start offset along the path (0 = path start, 1 = path end)
  startOffset: number;     // 0.0 to 1.0
  // Flip text to face outward (perpendicular to path center)
  flip: boolean;
  // Correct spacing for baseline alignment
  baselineOffset: number;  // px — distance above/below the path line
}

interface BezierSegment {
  type: "move" | "line" | "cubic" | "quadratic";
  start: { x: number; y: number };
  control1?: { x: number; y: number };  // for cubic
  control2?: { x: number; y: number };  // for cubic
  end: { x: number; y: number };
}
```

**Path binding UI:**
- A text element has an optional `pathId` property. When set, the text renders along the path instead of in a rectangular box.
- The path is a separate element (type: `"path"`) rendered on the canvas with visible handles for editing.
- To bind text to a path: select the text element → open the character panel (Plan 12) → "Text on Path" section → dropdown of all path elements on the canvas → select a path.
- The path element shows a badge "Bound: {text element name}" when it has a bound text.

**Text rendering along path:**

```ts
function layoutTextOnPath(
  content: RichTextContent,
  path: TextPath,
  baseStyles: SpanStyles,
  maxWidth: number
): PositionedGlyph[] {
  // 1. Measure each glyph using Canvas measureText
  // 2. Walk along the path using the bezier parametric equation
  //    For each glyph:
  //    a. Compute the cumulative distance along the path to the glyph start
  //    b. Get the point on the path at that distance (via binary search on t parameter)
  //    c. Get the tangent direction at that point (derivative of bezier)
  //    d. Compute the glyph rotation = atan2(tangent.y, tangent.x)
  //    e. Position the glyph with its baseline at path point + baselineOffset * normal
  //    f. If flip is true, rotate 180° and offset by -baselineOffset
  3. Return array of { glyph, x, y, rotation, styles } objects
}
```

**Rendering:** Each glyph is positioned via CSS `transform: translate(x, y) rotate(angle)` inside a container with `position: absolute`. The font shape is rendered via the standard `RichTextRenderer` per-glyph (each glyph = its own `<span>`).

**SVG falback rendering:** For complex paths with many glyphs, the container is an `<svg>` and each glyph is a `<text>` element with `transform` attribute. SVG handles complex transforms more efficiently than hundreds of CSS-transformed HTML spans for long curved text.

**Path offset UI:**
- `startOffset` slider (0.0–1.0) in the character panel (Plan 12) → moves the text start position along the path.
- `baselineOffset` numeric input (-50 to +50px) → moves text above/below the path line.
- `flip` checkbox → flips text orientation.


**Path editing UI:**
- When a path element is selected, its control points are rendered as draggable handles (circular `div`s, 8px diameter).
- Dragging a control point updates the bezier `control1`/`control2` or `start`/`end` position.
- The path line is rendered as a dashed line (`strokeDasharray: "4 4"`) when not selected, solid when selected.
- Snapping: control points snap to grid (if grid enabled) and to other element edges.

**i18n keys:**
- `typography.textOnPath.bindToPath` → "Bind to path"
- `typography.textOnPath.unbind` → "Unbind from path"
- `typography.textOnPath.startOffset` → "Start offset"
- `typography.textOnPath.baselineOffset` → "Baseline offset"
- `typography.textOnPath.flip` → "Flip text"
- `typography.textOnPath.noPath` → "No paths available"
- `typography.textOnPath.direction` → "Text direction"
- `typography.textOnPath.forward` → "Forward"
- `typography.textOnPath.reverse` → "Reverse"

### R5.10 Vertical Text

**File**: `frontend/common/views/dashboard/certificates/template-editor/canvas/text/VerticalText.tsx`

For Asian-style certificates with top-to-bottom text.

**Implementation:**
- Each character is placed in its own `CharacterBox` with `display: block; writing-mode: vertical-rl; text-orientation: mixed;`
- CSS `writing-mode: vertical-rl` handles the correct glyph orientation for CJK characters.
- For Latin characters in vertical mode: `text-orientation: sideways` rotates each letter 90° clockwise.
- Toggle in character panel (Plan 12) → `ParagraphStyles.vertical: boolean`.

**Mixed vertical/horizontal:** Certain characters (like numbers, Latin letters) in vertical text are rendered horizontally if `text-orientation: upright` is set. The property is per-paragraph.

### R5.11 Text Shadow on Canvas

Text shadow (defined in character properties, Plan 12) is rendered via CSS `text-shadow`:
```tsx
const textShadow = element.settings.textShadow
  ? `${element.settings.textShadow.x}px ${element.settings.textShadow.y}px ${element.settings.textShadow.blur}px ${alpha(color, opacity)}`
  : undefined;
```

**PDF parity:** The canvas `text-shadow` must match the PDF renderer's shadow emulation. Plan 06 handles the actual PDF shadow (since PDF doesn't support CSS `text-shadow` natively). The values (`x`, `y`, `blur`, `color`, `opacity`) are passed through unchanged.

### R5.12 Desktop vs Mobile Differences

| Feature | Desktop | Mobile |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Inline edit mode | Double-click → edit | Double-tap → edit |
| Text on path | Full path editing with draggable control points | Path selected → simplified edit dialog (slope/height sliders, no free-drag control points) |
| Text preview during drag | Toggle via `Ctrl+Shift+H` | Always simplified during touch drag |
| Text measurement tooltip | Shows during resize | Shows at bottom of element during resize |
| Vertical text | Supported via character panel toggle | Supported via edit dialog toggle |

### R5.13 Cross-Plan Contracts

- **Plan 06 (PDF)**: The `TextOverflowSettings`, `TextPath`, and vertical text `writing-mode` must be respected by the PDF renderer. The canvas and PDF must produce visually identical output. The PDF renderer receives the same `RichTextContent` and renders per-span styled text runs.
- **Plan 10**: The `RichTextRenderer` from Plan 10 is wrapped by the canvas `TextRenderer` defined here. The `RichTextToolbar` from Plan 10 appears during inline edit mode (§R5.7).
- **Plan 12**: The character panel defines `TextOverflowSettings` and `TextPath` properties on text elements. The canvas reads these from the store and renders accordingly.

### R5.14 Quality & Verification

**Per-file verification loop** (per AGENTS.md): Each new file must pass:
1. `bun run tsgo` — zero type errors
2. `bun biome:check` — zero formatting/lint issues
3. Lint via queue client: `curl -s -X POST http://localhost:${LINT_QUEUE_PORT}/lint -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"id":"r5p11-<file>","files":["<path>"]}'`
4. `bun run scripts/health/sub-loop.ts <file> --lifecycle lint`

**Instruction files to read**:
- `.agents/instructions/frontend.instructions.md`
- `frontend/views/AGENTS.md`, `frontend/AGENTS.md`
- `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md`

**Performance considerations**:
- Text measurement on every pixel change during drag is expensive. Cache measurements and invalidate only on content/bounds change.
- Text-on-path with >100 glyphs should switch to SVG rendering for performance.
- The text bitmap cache (§R5.5) must be primed on editor open (via `requestIdleCallback`) to avoid jank on first drag.
- The `OffscreenCanvas` API is only available in Chromium — provide fallback to a hidden `<canvas>` for non-Chromium browsers.

## Round 5: Context Menus & Right-Click Actions

> Added as Round 5 to extend the Plan 11 canvas with Photoshop/Illustrator-grade right-click context menus on the canvas surface, on selected elements, and on rulers. This section defines the canvas right-click menus, element right-click menus, ruler context menu, and the contextual-menu behavior rules (positioning, keyboard nav, theme, dismissal, smart filtering). Plan 11 imports the `contextMenuService` store, the `ContextMenuItem` type, and the `<ContextMenuHost>` React component from Plan 10 §R5.1 — it does not redefine those primitives. Plan 11 owns the *canvas-specific* menu builders, the *ruler* builder, and the chart of which items appear in which context.

### R5.1 Canvas Context Menu — Coordinate Capture & Positioning Hook

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/useCanvasContextMenu.ts` (new)

**Design**:

A hook attached to the canvas root SVG/div via `onContextMenu={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); openAt(e); }}`. The hook is responsible for:

1. Reading `useCanvasStore` (selection, clipboard, zoom, pan) via `useShallow` (only re-renders on those slices)
2. Computing the menu items via the builder (`buildCanvasContextMenu` §R5.2 or `buildElementContextMenu` §R5.3 depending on selection)
3. Calling `contextMenuService.openMenu('canvas', { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY }, items)`

```typescript
interface UseCanvasContextMenu {
  onContextMenu: (e: React.MouseEvent) => void;
  closeMenu: () => void;
}
```

**Coordinate translation**: The canvas tool needs the click in **canvas coordinates** (not just viewport coords) so paste-in-place, guide placement, and zoom-aware transforms land in the correct visual location. The hook converts `{x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY}` to canvas coords via the existing canvas viewport-to-canvas transform (`useCanvasStore.getState().viewportToCanvasPoint` from R4).

The viewport coords still drive menu positioning (because the host positions itself in viewport space); the canvas coords are passed in `item.data` (an `unknown` payload on `ContextMenuItem`) for actions that need the original click location in canvas space.

### R5.2 Canvas Context Menu — Empty Area (No Selection)

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/canvasContextMenu.ts` (new)

**Design**:

Built by `buildCanvasContextMenu(ctx)` when `selectionCount === 0` (or when the right-click hit no element, regardless of focus state). Menu items:

- **Paste** (visible only when `clipboardHasContent`; otherwise hidden — Adobe suppresses paste entries when clipboard is empty)
- **Paste in Place** (visible only when `clipboardHasContent`; pastes at original coordinates stored in clipboard)
- ——— separator
- **Select All** (Ctrl+A) — selects every unlocked, visible element on canvas
- **Deselect All** (Ctrl+Shift+A) — disabled when no selection; clears selection
- **Invert Selection** (visible when `selectionCount > 0` and totalUnlockVisible > selectionCount) — flips selection
- ——— separator
- **New Element** submenu: Text, Image, Shape, Line — each creates an element at the right-click canvas position (not centered)
- **Place...** — opens a file picker for image assets; places the result at click canvas coords
- ——— separator
- **Grid** submenu:
  - **Show Grid** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.gridVisible`)
  - **Snap to Grid** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.snapToGrid`)
  - **Grid Settings...** (opens grid settings dialog)
- **Guides** submenu:
  - **New Guide...** (opens new guide dialog positioned at the click — orientation inferred by whether the click was closer to horizontal/vertical ruler)
  - **Lock Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.lockGuides`)
  - **Clear Guides** (disabled when `guideStore.guides.length === 0`)
  - **Show Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.guidesVisible`) — `Ctrl+;`
  - **Snap to Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.snapToGuides`)
- ——— separator
- **Zoom In** (Ctrl++) — increments `canvasStore.zoom` by 25% (max 800%)
- **Zoom Out** (Ctrl+-) — decrements zoom by 25% (min 5%)
- **Fit on Screen** (`Ctrl+0`) — computes zoom to fit all elements
- **Actual Pixels** (`Ctrl+Alt+0`) — sets zoom = 100%
- **Print Size** — sets zoom so that 1 canvas unit = 1 CSS inch at 96 DPI / canvas DPI (from `CERT_CANVAS_DPI`)
- ——— separator
- **Document Setup...** — opens the document setup dialog (canvas dimensions, DPI, background color)
- **Canvas Properties...** — opens the canvas properties panel section (calls `setRightPanelTab('canvas')`)

Smart-filter rules (using `filterMenuItems` from Plan 10 §R5.3):
- Paste/Paste in Place hidden when `!clipboardHasContent`
- Invert Selection hidden when `selectionCount === 0` or no selectable-but-unselected remaining
- Snap/Grid items disabled (not hidden) when there are zero guides for guides-snap items (greyed out usable feedback)

### R5.3 Canvas Context Menu — Element(s) Selected

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/elementContextMenu.ts` (new)

**Design**:

Built by `buildElementContextMenu(ctx)` when one or more elements are selected and right-clicked (either on an element or on empty canvas while elements are selected). Menu items:

- **Cut** (`Ctrl+X`) — disabled when no selection; copies then deletes
- **Copy** (`Ctrl+C`) — disabled when no selection
- **Paste** (`Ctrl+V`) — pastes at cursor (offset 10,10 from cursor); visible only when `clipboardHasContent`
- **Paste in Front** (`Ctrl+F`) — pastes directly above topmost selected element in z-order
- **Paste in Back** (`Ctrl+B`) — pastes directly below bottommost selected element in z-order
- ——— separator
- **Bring to Front** (`Ctrl+Shift+]`) — z-order topmost
- **Bring Forward** (`Ctrl+]`) — up one slot
- **Send Backward** (`Ctrl+[`) — down one slot
- **Send to Back** (`Ctrl+Shift+[`) — z-order bottommost
- ——— separator
- **Duplicate** (`Ctrl+J`) — clones with 10px right/down offset; clones inherit all properties
- **Duplicate Special...** (`Ctrl+Alt+J`) — opens a dialog: number of copies, spacing (offset each), whether to keep transforms
- ——— separator
- **Group** (`Ctrl+G`) — disabled when `selectionCount <= 1` or all selected are groups
- **Ungroup** (`Ctrl+Shift+G`) — disabled when no selection is a group
- ——— separator
- **Lock** (`Ctrl+L`) — toggled; checked when all selected are locked; disabled when selection has mixed lock states (semi-checked Adobe behavior: shows indeterminate; we show check only when uniform)
- **Unlock** (`Ctrl+Alt+L`) — visible when any selected is locked (companion to Lock)
- **Unlock All on Canvas** — visible when any locked element exists anywhere on canvas
- ——— separator
- **Hide** (`Ctrl+,`) — hides selected (sets `element.visible = false`)
- **Show All** (`Ctrl+Alt+,`) — visible when any element on canvas is hidden
- ——— separator
- **Free Transform** (`Ctrl+T`) — enters free-transform mode (bounding box w/ rotate/scale handles from R3)
- **Transform** submenu:
  - **Rotate 90° CW** — rotates selected by +90° around center
  - **Rotate 90° CCW** — rotates by -90°
  - **Rotate 180°** — flips 180°
  - **Flip Horizontal** — `scaleX = -scaleX`
  - **Flip Vertical** — `scaleY = -scaleY`
  - **Numeric Transform...** — opens numeric transform dialog: X, Y, W, H, rotation, skew X, skew Y
- ——— separator
- **Align** submenu (visible when `selectionCount >= 2`):
  - **Left**, **Center Horizontal**, **Right** — align left edges / horizontal centers / right edges
  - **Top**, **Center Vertical**, **Bottom** — same vertical
  - Reference: aligns to bounding box of selection (or to canvas if `alignToCanvas` toggle is on)
- **Distribute** submenu (visible when `selectionCount >= 3`):
  - **Horizontal Centers** — equal horizontal spacing of centers
  - **Vertical Centers** — equal vertical spacing of centers
  - **Horizontal Space** — equal gaps between elements
  - **Vertical Space** — equal vertical gaps
- ——— separator
- **Edit in Photoshop / External Editor** — visible only when at least one selected is an image element; opens the source URL in the system-default image editor (where possible — falls back to "Open in new tab")
- **Replace Image...** — visible only when all selected are images; opens file picker
- **Export As Image** — visible only when exactly one element selected (any type); exports the element as PNG at 1x canvas-pixel resolution
- ——— separator
- **Properties...** — focuses the right panel on the selection (calls `setRightPanelTab('properties')` + scrolls to top)
- ——— separator
- **Delete** (`Del`) — `isDangerous: true`; shows Mini Confirm Dialog ("Delete N elements?", singular count adjusts message)

Smart-filter rules:
- All clipboard-flavored items hidden when `!clipboardHasContent`
- Group disabled when `selectionCount <= 1` or all selected are groups; Ungroup disabled when none selected is a group
- Lock toggle checked when all selected uniformly locked; mixed-state shows unchecked
- "Unlock All on Canvas", "Show All" hidden when no locked/hidden elements anywhere
- Rotate/Flip actions always present (work on any element type)
- Align submenu visible when `selectionCount >= 2`; Distribute submenu visible when `selectionCount >= 3`
- "Edit in Photoshop", "Replace Image" hidden unless selection includes image element(s)
- "Export As Image" disabled (not hidden) when `selectionCount !== 1`

### R5.4 Element-Specific Right-Click Additions

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/elementTypeMenuItems.ts` (new)

**Design**:

A pure function `elementTypeMenuItems(elementType: CanvasElementType, ctx: MenuContextDescriptor): ContextMenuItem[]` that produces per-element-type additions appended to the element context menu (§R5.3) after a leading separator. These are owned by Plan 11 because they're defined per element type — but the actual property editing UI lives in Plan 12. Plan 11 owns only the **menu item declaration** (label, shortcut, action signature); the action handlers all dispatch into the canvas store or `templateElementEditorStore` (Plan 12 owner).

```typescript
export function elementTypeMenuItems(elementType: CanvasElementType, ctx: MenuContextDescriptor): ContextMenuItem[];
```

**Text element** additions:

- ——— separator
- **Edit Text** (`Enter`) — places the text element in edit mode (cursor inside the text)
- **Change Font** submenu:
  - **Recent Fonts** (visible when `uiStore.recentFonts.length > 0`, up to 5 items)
  - ——— separator (inside submenu)
  - **Browse All...** (opens the font browser picker dialog)
- **Increase Font Size** (`Ctrl+Shift+>``) — `fontSize += 2pt`
- **Decrease Font Size** (`Ctrl+Shift+<`) — `fontSize -= 2pt` (floor at 1pt)
- ——— separator
- **Align Text** submenu: Left (`Ctrl+Shift+L`), Center (`Ctrl+Shift+C`), Right (`Ctrl+Shift+R`), Justify (`Ctrl+Shift+J`)
- **Bold** (`Ctrl+B`) — toggle, checked when fontWeight ≥ 700
- **Italic** (`Ctrl+I`) — toggle, checked when fontStyle is italic
- **Underline** (`Ctrl+U`) — toggle, checked when textDecoration includes underline
- ——— separator
- **Convert to Outlines** — turns text into editable shape path(s) (one `<path>` per glyph)
- **Convert to Path** — opens the text-on-path editor (Toggle onto a path,s render text along a contour)

**Image element** additions:

- ——— separator
- **Replace Image...** — opens file picker
- **Extract Image** — pulls the image URL/bytes out of the element and adds it to the asset library (removes it from the element but keeps the element with placeholder)
- ——— separator
- **Edit Externally** — opens the source URL in the OS default image editor / browser
- **Reset Adjustments** — clears brightness/contrast/saturation/etc. effect filters on the element
- ——— separator
- **Crop to Shape** — enters crop mode (interactive handle overlay)
- **Set as Background** — moves the image to a dedicated background layer behind all other elements (sets z-index to MIN, marks `isBackground: true`)

**Shape element** additions:

- ——— separator
- **Edit Shape** — enters shape edit mode (renders anchor points on canvas; user can drag them)
- **Change Shape Type** submenu:
  - Rectangle (`Ctrl+Shift+R`), Rounded Rectangle (`Ctrl+Alt+Shift+R`), Ellipse (`Ctrl+Shift+E`), Polygon (`Ctrl+Shift+P`), Star (`Ctrl+Shift+S`), Triangle (`Ctrl+Shift+T`), Line (`Ctrl+Shift+L`)
  - Each morphs the path while preserving the element's bounds (anchor count may change)
- ——— separator
- **Boolean Operation** submenu (visible when `selectionCount >= 2`):
  - **Unite** (`Ctrl+Shift+U`) — union of paths
  - **Subtract** (`Ctrl+Shift+S`) — subtract back from front
  - **Intersect** (`Ctrl+Shift+I`) — intersection only
  - **Exclude** (`Ctrl+Shift+E`) — XOR
  - **Divide** (`Ctrl+Shift+D`) — splits at overlaps into separate shapes
  - **Merge** (`Ctrl+Shift+M`) — like Unite but preserves strokes per region
- **Flatten** — converts a boolean compound into a single SVG path
- ——— separator
- **Convert to Outlines** — turns filled shape into outline-only (fills become strokes)

**Group element** additions:

- ——— separator
- **Enter Isolation Mode** (also achievable by double-clicking the group) — zooms into group bounds and dims siblings — `uiStore.setIsolationDepth(depth)`
- **Ungroup** — dissolves the group (same as `Ctrl+Shift+G` but easier once in isolation)
- ——— separator
- **Group Properties...** — opens a small dialog showing the group's name, child count, bounding box W×H, color tag — i.e. the same dialog as Layer Properties but for the group

### R5.5 Ruler Context Menu

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/rulerContextMenu.ts` (new)

**Design**:

Built by `buildRulerContextMenu(opts: { orientation: 'horizontal' | 'vertical'; hasGuides: boolean; anyLockedGuides: boolean })`. The orientation is inferred from which ruler the user right-clicked (top = horizontal, left = vertical). The `New Guide` default orientation matches the ruler orientation.

Menu items:

- **New Guide...** — opens a dialog with orientation pre-set to the ruler's orientation and position prefilled with the click's orthogonal canvas coordinate (so a horizontal ruler right-click at x=320 prefills position = 320)
- ——— separator
- **Units** submenu (radio-like, checked circles on active): Pixels, Inches, cm (lowercased in submenu label per i18n), mm, Picas, Points — each sets `uiStore.rulerUnits` and reflects across rulers + measurements
- ——— separator
- **Show Rulers** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.rulersVisible`) — `Ctrl+R`
- **Show Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.guidesVisible`) — `Ctrl+;`
- **Show Grid** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.gridVisible`) — `Ctrl+'`
- **Snap to Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.snapToGuides`) — `Ctrl+Shift+;`
- **Snap to Grid** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.snapToGrid`) — `Ctrl+Shift+'`
- ——— separator
- **Lock Guides** (toggle, checked when `uiStore.lockGuides`) — disables guide dragging
- **Clear Guides** (disabled when `guideStore.guides.length === 0`)
- ——— separator
- **Reset Ruler Origin** — resets the ruler origin to (0,0) top-left (also achievable by double-clicking the corner of the rulers)

**Implementation**: The ruler root box (`EditorRulerTop.tsx`, `EditorRulerSide.tsx` from R4) attaches `onContextMenu` calling `buildRulerContextMenu({ orientation, hasGuides, anyLockedGuides })` then `contextMenuService.openMenu('ruler-' + orientation, { x, y }, items)`. The menu position is anchored at the click; smart filtering handles disabled rules.

### R5.6 Duplicate Special Dialog

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/dialogs/DuplicateSpecialDialog.tsx` (new)

**Design**:

Invoked from `Duplicate Special...` in the element context menu (§R5.3). A MUI v9 `Dialog` with:

- **Number of Copies** — `TextField` with `type="number"`, min 1, max 100 (warn at high values via helperText)
- **Spacing** — composite field: X offset (px) and Y offset (px), each separately; or `Tab` toggle between "Translate" (offset each) or "Rotate" (rotation angle per copy around center)
- **Scale per copy** — optional secondary slider (100% = no scale change, 0-200% allowable)
- **Apply to** preview shows the first 3 copies as outlined rectangles on a mini canvas preview
- Confirm button dispatches `canvasStore.duplicateSpecial(selectionIds, { count, spacing, mode, scale })` — the store handler clones the selection N times with incremental transforms.

All `sx={{}}` — no style props. All colors from `theme.palette`. All labels via `useAppTranslation('certificateEditor')`.

### R5.7 Numeric Transform Dialog

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/dialogs/NumericTransformDialog.tsx` (new)

**Design**:

Invoked from `Transform → Numeric Transform...` in the element context menu. A MUI v9 `Dialog` with `TextField` inputs for:

- X (px), Y (px) — element top-left in canvas coordinates
- W (px), H (px) — width/height; toggles a lock-aspect-ratio chain icon
- Rotation (°) — -360 to 360
- Skew X (°), Skew Y (°) — -45 to 45
- Flip H, Flip V — checkbox toggles

Preview applies live to the selected element via `canvasStore.updateElementTransform(id, transform)` as the user types (debounced 100ms). Confirm commits; Cancel reverts to the original transform (snapshot on open).

i18n keys: `transformDialog.title`, `...x`, `...y`, `...width`, `...height`, `...lockAspect`, `...rotation`, `...skewX`, `...skewY`, `...flipH`, `...flipV`, `...reset`, `...apply`.

### R5.8 Canvas Behavior & Theme

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/templates/editor/contextMenus/contextMenuBehavior.ts` (new — docs/util module)

**Design**:

A documentation module mirroring the behavior rules listed in this design: menu position stays on screen, dismisses on outside click, Esc, and scroll; submenu delay 200ms; keyboard nav arrow keys + Enter + Esc; dark theme aware; persists until dismissed; smart filtering.

The file exports constants:

```typescript
export const SUBMENU_DELAY_MS = 200;
export const SUBMENU_ROLLBACK_MS = 150;
export const MENU_OPEN_TRANSITION_MS = 80;
export const MENU_CLOSE_TRANSITION_MS = 80;
```

These are read by the Plan 10 `<ContextMenuHost>` and `SubmenuTrigger` to ensure iOS/Android/MAT behavior is consistent with Adobe products. The values are co-located here so Plans 10 + 11 reference the same constants.

### R5.9 Contextual Menu Behavior Rules (Specification)

The behavior matrix governs every menu instance in this plan:

| Rule | Spec | Implementation ref |
|---|---|---|
| Contextual | Items adapt to current selection / clipboard / panel state | `filterMenuItems` (Plan 10 §R5.3) + `useMenuContextDescriptor` (Plan 10 §R5.4) |
| Disabled items | Visible but greyed (not hidden) for cut/copy/clear-guides; *hidden* for paste / image items / invert selection | §R5.2, §R5.3 |
| Submenu delay | 200ms hover on parent before expanding; 150ms rollback after mouse leaves parent | `SubmenuTrigger` (Plan 10 §R5.12), constants from §R5.8 |
| Keyboard navigation | Arrow keys navigate, Enter selects, Esc closes; ArrowRight opens submenu, ArrowLeft collapses | `useMenuKeyboardNav` (Plan 10 §R5.15) |
| Menu position | Open at cursor (right-click location), stays on screen (flip if overflow) | `ContextMenuHost` (Plan 10 §R5.2) |
| Dark theme | Matches theme.palette.mode — `background.paper`, `text.primary` are sourced from theme | `contextMenuPaperSx` (Plan 10 §R5.13) |
| Menu persists | Click outside, Esc, window blur, canvas scroll — any closes the menu | `useOutsideClickClose` (Plan 10 §R5.14) |
| Smart item filtering | Image-only items hidden for non-image selections; align/distribute hidden when count below threshold | §R5.3, §R5.4 |

